{"qid": "tq:dpql_1648", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "The composer is **Richard Wagner**.\n\nWagner founded the Bayreuth Festival specifically to stage his own works, and the town remains synonymous with his operas to this day. The festival theater (Festspielhaus) was built to his specifications and continues to host annual performances of his works, particularly the *Ring Cycle* and *Parsifal*.\n\nAnswer: Richard Wagner", "correct": true, "gold": "Richard WAGNER"}
{"qid": "tq:dpql_1648", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "Bayreuth, Germany, is home to the annual Bayreuth Festival, held in the Festspielhaus theater that Richard Wagner himself designed and had built specifically for the performance of his operas (most famously the Ring cycle).\nAnswer: Richard Wagner", "correct": true, "gold": "Richard WAGNER"}
