{"qid": "tq:qw_984", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "The term for these marks is **hallmark** (or **hallmarks**).\n\nHallmarks are official stamps applied to precious metal items (gold, silver, platinum) by assay offices to certify the metal's purity, identify the testing office, and indicate the year of assay. The practice originated at Goldsmiths' Hall in London in the 14th century, hence the name. A complete set typically includes a standard mark (purity), an assay office mark, a date letter, and often a maker's mark.\n\nAnswer: hallmark (or hallmarks)", "correct": true, "gold": "Hall Mark"}
{"qid": "tq:qw_984", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "MAI-Thinking-1", "resp": "Answer: Hallmark", "correct": true, "gold": "Hall Mark"}
