{"qid": "tq:qw_984", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "A hallmark is the official term used for precious metal items (chiefly gold and silver). By definition it consists of a grouped series of stamped symbols applied at an assay office; these symbols collectively certify the metal\u2019s fineness (i.e., its genuineness) and normally include a date letter that records the year in which the assay and marking took place. The same set of marks may also contain an office or sponsor\u2019s mark, but the core legal function remains authentication of purity and the year of testing. Hence the word that precisely names \u201ca set of marks\u201d with those two attributes is \u201challmark.\u201d\nAnswer: hallmark", "correct": true, "gold": "Hall Mark"}
{"qid": "tq:qw_6209", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "The quest for the Golden Fleece is one of the best-known episodes in Greek mythology. Jason, son of the rightful king of Iolcus, was sent by the usurper Pelias to retrieve the fleece from the distant land of Colchis. To accomplish this, he assembled a crew of the foremost heroes of the age (including Heracles, Orpheus, the Dioscuri, Peleus, Telamon, and many others) and sailed aboard the specially built ship *Argo*. Because they voyaged on the *Argo*, the company is collectively known as the Argonauts (\u201csailors on the Argo\u201d).\nThus the band of heroes who accompanied Jason is the Argonauts.\nAnswer: the Argonauts", "correct": true, "gold": "Argonauts"}
{"qid": "tq:qw_6209", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "These heroes were known as the **Argonauts**, named after their ship, the *Argo*, which was built by Argus with the help of Athena. The band included many famous figures from Greek mythology, such as Heracles (Hercules), Orpheus, Castor and Pollux (the Dioscuri), Peleus, Telamon, and Atalanta.\n\nAnswer: The Argonauts", "correct": true, "gold": "Argonauts"}
{"qid": "tq:qw_6209", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "MAI-Thinking-1", "resp": "Answer: The Argonauts", "correct": true, "gold": "Argonauts"}
