{"qid": "tq:qg_2424", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "The most common variants of pool (also called pocket billiards) are eight-ball, nine-ball, and straight pool (14.1 continuous). Each uses a different number of object balls and therefore a different racking shape:\n- Eight-ball and straight pool both rack 15 balls inside a triangular frame.\n- Nine-ball uses only the balls numbered 1\u20139; these nine balls fit precisely into a compact diamond-shaped frame (rows of 1-2-3-2-1).\nBecause the diamond pattern is the defining rack geometry for nine balls, the game that employs it is nine-ball.\nAnswer: nine-ball (9-ball)", "correct": true, "gold": "Nine-ball"}
