{"qid": "tq:qw_1201", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "The question specifies a multi-day rowing regatta on the River Thames whose dates fall on the Wednesday-to-Sunday period straddling the first weekend in July.  \n\nThe only event that matches all of these constraints is the Henley Royal Regatta, held annually at Henley-on-Thames. Other well-known Thames fixtures can be ruled out quickly:  \n- The Oxford\u2013Cambridge Boat Race occurs in late March or early April and lasts only a single afternoon.  \n- The Head of the River Race is a one-day processional event, also held in March or April.  \n- Various local \u201chead\u201d races or sculling competitions occupy single weekends scattered throughout the year and do not run for five consecutive days in early July.  \n\nThus the description points unambiguously to the Henley Royal Regatta.\n\nAnswer: Henley Royal Regatta", "correct": true, "gold": "Henley Royal Regatta"}
