{"qid": "tq:dpql_1443", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "The **left-hand rule** for predicting the direction of motion (force) in an electric motor is **Fleming's Left-Hand Rule**, named after British engineer **John Ambrose Fleming**.\n\nIn this rule: the **first finger** points in the direction of the magnetic field (N\u2192S), the **second finger** points in the direction of conventional current, and the **thumb** points in the direction of the force/motion on the conductor.\n\nAnswer: Fleming (or John Ambrose Fleming)", "correct": true, "gold": "John Ambrose Fleming"}
{"qid": "tq:dpql_1443", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "Cohere-command-a-plus-05-2026", "resp": "<|START_TEXT|>Fleming's left-hand rule, which predicts the direction of motion in an electric motor, is named after Sir John Ambrose Fleming.\n\nAnswer: Sir John Ambrose Fleming<|END_TEXT|>", "correct": true, "gold": "John Ambrose Fleming"}
