{"qid": "tq:bb_3448", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "openai/gpt-5.4", "resp": "In a standard perm, after winding the hair, applying the waving lotion, processing, and rinsing, the usual final stage is **neutralising** (also called fixing), which reforms the hair\u2019s bonds to set the new curl shape.\n\nAnswer: Neutralising the hair.", "correct": false, "gold": "Neutralizing"}
{"qid": "tq:bb_3448", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "DeepSeek-V4-Flash", "resp": "The final stage of a hair perming process is generally **neutralizing** (or applying a neutralizer). This step stops the action of the perming solution and re-hardens the disulfide bonds in the hair into their new, curled shape.\n\nAnswer: Neutralizing", "correct": true, "gold": "Neutralizing"}
