{"qid": "tq:dpql_1726", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "The major suits in Bridge are **spades** (\u2660) and **hearts** (\u2665). \n\nThey are distinguished from the minor suits (diamonds and clubs) because they score higher (30 points per trick versus 20) and require fewer tricks to make a game contract (4-level versus 5-level).\n\nAnswer: Spades and hearts.", "correct": false, "gold": "Hearts and Spades"}
{"qid": "tq:dpql_1726", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "In the card game of Bridge (contract bridge), a standard deck has four suits that are divided into two categories for bidding and scoring purposes: major suits and minor suits. The major suits rank higher in the bidding hierarchy and score more points when making contracts.\n\nAnswer: Spades and hearts", "correct": false, "gold": "Hearts and Spades"}
