{"qid": "tq:bb_3448", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "The hair perming process typically involves wrapping hair around rods, applying a chemical reducing agent (perm solution) to break the hair's disulfide bonds, and then rebuilding those bonds in the new curled shape. \n\nThe final stage of this chemical process is **neutralisation** (or neutralization), where a hydrogen peroxide-based neutralizer is applied to oxidize and reform the disulfide bonds, permanently \"locking\" the hair into its new curled shape around the rods. After the neutralizer has processed, the hair is rinsed, the rods are removed, and the hair is styled.\n\nAnswer: Neutralisation (applying the neutralizer to set the new curl pattern).", "correct": false, "gold": "Neutralizing"}
