nswer: flageolet", "correct": true, "gold": "FLAGEOLET"}
{"qid": "tq:odql_9283", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "openai/gpt-5.4", "resp": "Primula veris is the **cowslip**, a common meadow flower in Europe.\n\nAnswer: Cowslip", "correct": true, "gold": "COWSLIP"}
{"qid": "tq:tc_2901", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "The pancreas secretes **insulin** and **glucagon** to regulate blood sugar. Beta cells in the islets of Langerhans release insulin when blood glucose is high (promoting glucose uptake and storage), while alpha cells release glucagon when blood glucose is low (promoting glycogen breakdown and glucose release). These hormones work antagonistically to maintain glucose homeostasis.\n\nAnswer: Insulin and glucagon.", "correct": true, "gold": "Insulin"}
{"qid": "tq:odql_9283", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "DeepSeek-V4-Flash", "resp": "Primula veris is the Latin name for the cowslip.\n\nAnswer: cowslip", "correct": true, "gold": "COWSLIP"}
{"qid": "tq:odql_9283", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "Primula veris is commonly known as the **cowslip** (also called common cowslip). It is a yellow-flowered perennial plant native to Europe and western Asia, often found in meadows and pastures.\n\nAnswer: cowslip", "correct": true, "gold": "COWSLIP"}
{"qid": "tq:tc_2901", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "Cohere-command-a-plus-05-2026", "resp": "<|START_TEXT|>The pancreas produces several hormones that help control blood glucose. Beta cells release insulin, which lowers blood sugar by promoting glucose uptake into cells and storage. Alpha cells release glucagon, which raises blood sugar by stimulating the liver to produce glucose when levels drop too low. Together, these hormones maintain stable blood sugar levels.\n\nAnswer: Insulin (and glucagon) are the hormones secreted by the pancreas to regulate blood sugar levels.<|END_TEXT|>", "correct": true, "gold": "Insulin"}
{"qid": "tq:odql_9283", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "Cowslip (a common yellow wildflower of the primrose family).\nAnswer: cowslip", "correct": true, "gold": "COWSLIP"}
{"qid": "tq:odql_9283", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5", "resp": "Primula veris is the Latin name for **Cowslip**.\n\nAnswer: Cowslip", "correct": true, "gold": "COWSLIP"}
{"qid": "tq:tc_2901", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5", "resp": "The pancreas secretes two main hormones to regulate blood sugar levels:\n\n1. **Insulin** - produced by beta cells in the islets of Langerhans; it lowers blood sugar by helping cells absorb glucose from the bloodstream and promoting glucose storage as glycogen in the liver and muscles.\n\n2. **Glucagon** - produced by alpha cells in the islets of Langerhans; it raises blood sugar by signaling the liver to convert stored glycogen back into glucose and release it into the bloodstream.\n\nThese two hormones work together in a feedback system to keep blood glucose levels balanced.\n\nAnswer: Insulin and glucagon", "correct": true, "gold": "Insulin"}
{"qid": "tq:tc_2901", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "MAI-Thinking-1", "resp": "Answer: Insulin and glucagon", "correct": true, "gold": "Insulin"}
