{"qid": "tq:odql_557", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "In the imperial system, the conversion is:\n- 1 gallon = 4 quarts\n- 1 quart = 2 pints\n- 1 pint = 4 gills\n\nTherefore: 1 gallon = 4 \u00d7 2 \u00d7 4 = **32 gills**\n\nAlternatively, using fluid ounces: 1 imperial gallon = 160 fluid ounces and 1 imperial gill = 5 fluid ounces, so 160 \u00f7 5 = 32.\n\nAnswer: 32", "correct": true, "gold": "32"}
{"qid": "tq:odql_557", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "In the imperial system of measurement, volume units are related as follows:\n- 1 imperial gallon = 4 quarts\n- 1 quart = 2 pints, so 1 gallon = 8 pints\n- 1 imperial pint = 4 gills (or equivalently, 1 gill = 5 imperial fluid ounces and 1 pint = 20 imperial fluid ounces)\nMultiplying through therefore gives 8 pints/gallon \u00d7 4 gills/pint = 32 gills per gallon. (The same count of 32 holds in US customary units, though the absolute sizes of the units differ.)\nAnswer: 32", "correct": true, "gold": "32"}
