{"qid": "tq:dpql_3475", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "MAI-Thinking-1", "resp": "The historical subject matter of Arthur Miller's *The Crucible* is the **Salem witch trials** of 1692\u20131693 in colonial Massachusetts. \r\n\r\nDuring this period, mass hysteria led to the accusation, trial, and execution of numerous people\u2014mostly women\u2014who were accused of practicing witchcraft. Miller used these events as an allegory for the anti-communist Red Scare and McCarthyism of his own time. \r\n\r\nAnswer: The Salem witch trials of 1692\u20131693 in colonial Massachusetts.", "correct": true, "gold": "Salem Witch Trials"}
{"qid": "tq:jp_2062", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "Munich (M\u00fcnchen), Germany, is the birthplace of Oktoberfest. The festival began there in 1810 as a public celebration of the wedding between Crown Prince Ludwig (later King Ludwig I) and Princess Therese of Saxony-Hildburghausen, held on the Theresienwiese grounds. It has been held annually in Munich ever since (with only a few interruptions), establishing it as the original event; other cities host imitations or spin-offs.\nAnswer: Munich", "correct": true, "gold": "Munich"}
{"qid": "tq:jp_2062", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "The original Oktoberfest is celebrated in **Munich, Germany**. It began in 1810 as a wedding celebration for Crown Prince Ludwig and Princess Therese, and takes place annually on the Theresienwiese grounds in late September through the first weekend in October.\n\nAnswer: Munich", "correct": true, "gold": "Munich"}
{"qid": "tq:jp_2062", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "Cohere-command-a-plus-05-2026", "resp": "<|START_TEXT|>The original Oktoberfest, which began in 1810, is celebrated in Munich, Germany.  \nAnswer: Munich<|END_TEXT|>", "correct": true, "gold": "Munich"}
{"qid": "tq:odql_15045", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "The eleventh labour of Heracles was to obtain the golden apples of the Hesperides. Ladon was the hundred-headed dragon that coiled around the tree bearing these apples in the garden at the edge of the world, and Heracles killed him (typically by shooting him with arrows) to retrieve the fruit.\n\nAnswer: The eleventh labour (obtaining the golden apples of the Hesperides).", "correct": true, "gold": "The apples of the Hesperides"}
{"qid": "tq:jp_2062", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5", "resp": "Oktoberfest originated in Munich, Germany in 1810, celebrating the royal wedding of Crown Prince Ludwig (later King Ludwig I) to Princess Therese of Saxe-Hildburghausen. It has continued as an annual tradition ever since.\n\nAnswer: Munich, Germany", "correct": true, "gold": "Munich"}
