{"qid": "tq:bb_2843", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "The wasabi plant (Eutrema japonicum) produces an enlarged underground stem known as a rhizome. This rhizome is harvested, peeled, and finely grated to produce the familiar pungent green paste used as a condiment; the leaves and petioles are edible but are not the source of the paste.\nAnswer: rhizome (rootstock)", "correct": false, "gold": "Roots"}
