{"qid": "tq:qw_669", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "The state described is **Nirvana** (or Nibbana in Pali). In Buddhist teaching, Nirvana is the ultimate liberation from the cycle of rebirth (samsara), characterized by the extinction of craving, hatred, and delusion. It represents the cessation of suffering and the attainment of perfect peace, bliss, and freedom from the necessity of future births. While the living experience of this liberation is sometimes distinguished as \"nirvana with remainder,\" the final state upon death\u2014complete release from the conditioned world\u2014is the ultimate goal of Buddhist practice.\n\nAnswer: Nirvana", "correct": true, "gold": "Nirvana"}
{"qid": "tq:jp_165", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "Carmen Miranda's signature look in films and performances featured an elaborate headdress piled high with artificial tropical fruits (bananas, pineapples, grapes, etc.).\nAnswer: fruit (tropical fruits)", "correct": true, "gold": "Fruit"}
