{"qid": "tq:sfq_12368", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "Highclere Castle is the ancestral home of the Earl of Carnarvon and has been used extensively as a filming location for period dramas. Its exterior, state rooms, and grounds match the fictional Yorkshire estate of Downton Abbey so closely that the producers of the ITV1 series chose it as the principal location for both interiors and exteriors across all six seasons. Although the original run concluded in 2015, the programme remains the production most directly and continuously associated with the castle, and the question\u2019s reference to a \u201ccurrent ITV1 series\u201d aligns with the period when Downton Abbey was still in production and transmission on that channel.\n\nAnswer: Downton Abbey", "correct": true, "gold": "Downton Abbey"}
