{"qid": "tq:qw_16501", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "openai/gpt-5.4", "resp": "Warren Hastings was appointed under **King George III**. He became the first Governor of the Presidency of Fort William (Bengal) and head of the Supreme Council of Bengal under the **Regulating Act of 1773**, during George III\u2019s reign.\n\nAnswer: King George III", "correct": true, "gold": "George III"}
{"qid": "tq:qw_16501", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "DeepSeek-V4-Flash", "resp": "Warren Hastings was appointed as the first Governor-General of the Presidency of Fort William (Bengal) under the Regulating Act of 1773. The British monarch at that time was King George III.\n\nAnswer: George III", "correct": true, "gold": "George III"}
{"qid": "tq:odql_13429", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "The Humber Estuary is formed by the confluence of the Yorkshire Ouse and the Trent. Further downstream, at Kingston upon Hull, the much smaller River Hull joins the estuary; this meeting point is known locally as Sammy\u2019s Point. The Deep aquarium occupies a purpose-built building precisely on that promontory, making the River Hull the watercourse whose confluence with the Humber is in question.\nAnswer: River Hull", "correct": true, "gold": "(River) HULL"}
{"qid": "tq:odql_13429", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5", "resp": "Answer: River Hull", "correct": true, "gold": "(River) HULL"}
{"qid": "tq:qw_16501", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "Cohere-command-a-plus-05-2026", "resp": "<|START_TEXT|>Answer: King George III<|END_TEXT|>", "correct": true, "gold": "George III"}
{"qid": "tq:qw_16501", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "Warren Hastings was appointed as the first Governor-General of India (Governor of the Presidency of Fort William and head of the Supreme Council of Bengal) in 1773 under the Regulating Act. This occurred during the reign of **King George III**, who was monarch from 1760 to 1820.\n\nAnswer: George III", "correct": true, "gold": "George III"}
{"qid": "tq:qw_11123", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "openai/gpt-5.4", "resp": "Michael Phelps represented the **United States** at the 2012 Summer Olympics.\n\nAnswer: United States", "correct": true, "gold": "USA"}
{"qid": "tq:qw_16501", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5", "resp": "Warren Hastings was appointed in 1772, during the reign of King George III.\n\nAnswer: George III", "correct": true, "gold": "George III"}
{"qid": "tq:qw_16501", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "The Regulating Act of 1773 (passed by the British Parliament) created the post of Governor-General of the Presidency of Fort William and vested it with authority over the other presidencies. Warren Hastings, already Governor of Bengal since 1772, was named the first incumbent and took office in 1774.  \n\nAt that date the reigning sovereign was George III (r. 1760\u20131820). No later monarch\u2014least of all Queen Victoria, whose assumption of the title Empress of India lay almost a century in the future\u2014could have made the appointment.\n\nAnswer: George III", "correct": true, "gold": "George III"}
