{"qid": "tq:sfq_6943", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "To find the highest prime number less than 100, I check numbers downward from 99:\n\n- **99**: Divisible by 3 (9+9=18), so not prime.\n- **98**: Even number, divisible by 2, so not prime.\n- **97**: Check divisibility by primes up to \u221a97 \u2248 9.8 (i.e., 2, 3, 5, 7):\n  - Not divisible by 2 (it's odd)\n  - Not divisible by 3 (9+7=16, not divisible by 3)\n  - Not divisible by 5 (doesn't end in 0 or 5)\n  - Not divisible by 7 (97 = 7\u00d713 + 6, remainder 6)\n\nSince 97 has no divisors other than 1 and itself, it is prime.\n\nAnswer: 97", "correct": true, "gold": "97"}
{"qid": "tq:sfq_6943", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "A prime number greater than 1 has no divisors other than 1 and itself. Checking downward from 99:\n- 99 = 9 \u00d7 11 (composite)\n- 98 is even (composite)\n- 97 has no divisors among primes \u2264 7 (its square root is ~9.85), so it is prime.\nThus 97 is the largest prime below 100.\nAnswer: 97", "correct": true, "gold": "97"}
{"qid": "tq:sfq_6943", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "Cohere-command-a-plus-05-2026", "resp": "<|START_TEXT|>The prime numbers less than 100 are those integers greater than 1 that have no positive divisors other than 1 and themselves. Checking from 99 downwards, we find that 99 = 9 \u00d7 11 (not prime), 98 = 2 \u00d7 49 (not prime), 97 has no divisors other than 1 and 97, making it prime. All numbers lower than 97 are either composite or smaller primes. Therefore, the highest prime number less than 100 is 97.\n\nAnswer: 97<|END_TEXT|>", "correct": true, "gold": "97"}
{"qid": "tq:sfq_6943", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5", "resp": "97 is prime (not divisible by 2, 3, 5, or 7), and 98, 99 are not prime.\n\nAnswer: 97", "correct": true, "gold": "97"}
