{"qid": "tq:sfq_11249", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "Jim Bowen (born Peter Williams) began his working life with a series of manual and short-term jobs: painter and decorator, market trader, and a spell of National Service in the army. After qualifying as a teacher at the City of Leeds Training College he took a permanent post in a Lancashire secondary school, where he taught for several years while performing stand-up comedy in working-men\u2019s clubs in the evenings. He eventually left the classroom to become a full-time comedian and, later, the host of Bullseye. In biographical sources the occupation most consistently cited as the one immediately preceding his comedy career is therefore schoolteacher.\nAnswer: schoolteacher (or teacher)", "correct": true, "gold": "Teacher"}
