{"qid": "tq:bt_3772", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "The theme music was the **\"Colonel Bogey March\"** (also referred to as the \"River Kwai March\"). Originally composed by Kenneth J. Alford in 1914, it was adapted by Malcolm Arnold for the 1957 film and became famous for the scene where the British prisoners whistle the tune while marching into the camp. Arnold won an Academy Award for his score.\n\nAnswer: Colonel Bogey March (also known as River Kwai March)", "correct": true, "gold": "Colonel Bogey"}
