{"qid": "tq:bt_105", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "A manse is a residence (typically a large house) provided for the use of a minister, especially in Presbyterian, Methodist, or other Protestant denominations. This distinguishes it from related terms such as rectory (for a rector), vicarage (for a vicar), or presbytery (for a Catholic priest).  \n\nThus the profession whose member would live in a manse is a minister (or clergyman/pastor).  \n\nAnswer: minister (clergyman/pastor)", "correct": true, "gold": "Clergyman"}
{"qid": "tq:bt_3772", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "The 1957 film *The Bridge on the River Kwai* prominently features the \u201cColonel Bogey March\u201d (composed in 1914 by Kenneth J. Alford). Prisoners whistle it as they enter the camp, and it became the movie\u2019s instantly recognizable theme; Malcolm Arnold later arranged it with an original counter-march for the soundtrack.\n\nAnswer: Colonel Bogey March", "correct": true, "gold": "Colonel Bogey"}
{"qid": "tq:sfq_17938", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5", "resp": "The oboe traditionally plays the tuning note (A) at the start of an orchestral performance, as its clear, penetrating tone is easy for other musicians to match.\n\nAnswer: Oboe", "correct": true, "gold": "OBOE"}
