{"qid": "tq:sfq_17938", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "The standard practice in a symphony orchestra is for the principal oboist to sound a concert A (typically at 440 Hz). This note is chosen because the oboe\u2019s double-reed timbre is penetrating and stable in pitch, allowing the entire ensemble\u2014starting with the concertmaster and then the other strings, winds, and brass\u2014to tune reliably to it before the performance begins.\nAnswer: oboe", "correct": true, "gold": "OBOE"}
