{"qid": "tq:sfq_2368", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "Reinhard Heydrich was appointed head of the Gestapo in 1936 when Heinrich Himmler reorganized the German police system. While Himmler remained the overall chief of police as Reichsf\u00fchrer-SS and Chief of German Police, Heydrich became the operational head of the Gestapo (and Kripo) as Chief of the Security Police, a position he held until his assassination in 1942.\n\nAnswer: Reinhard Heydrich", "correct": false, "gold": "Heinrich Himmler"}
