{"qid": "tq:qb_2546", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "openai/gpt-5.4", "resp": "For an \\(n\\)-sided polygon, the sum of the interior angles is \\((n-2)\\times 180^\\circ\\).\n\nA hexagon has \\(6\\) sides, so:\n\n\\[\n(6-2)\\times 180^\\circ = 4\\times 180^\\circ = 720^\\circ\n\\]\n\nAnswer: 720\u00b0", "correct": true, "gold": "720"}
{"qid": "tq:qb_2546", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "DeepSeek-V4-Flash", "resp": "The sum of interior angles of a polygon with \\(n\\) sides is given by \\((n-2) \\times 180^\\circ\\). For a hexagon, \\(n = 6\\).\n\n\\[\n(6-2) \\times 180^\\circ = 4 \\times 180^\\circ = 720^\\circ\n\\]\n\nAnswer: 720", "correct": true, "gold": "720"}
{"qid": "tq:qb_2546", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5", "resp": "The sum of interior angles of a polygon is calculated using (n-2) \u00d7 180\u00b0, where n is the number of sides.\n\nFor a hexagon: (6-2) \u00d7 180\u00b0 = 4 \u00d7 180\u00b0 = 720\u00b0\n\nAnswer: 720", "correct": true, "gold": "720"}
{"qid": "tq:qb_2546", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "The sum of interior angles of a polygon with $n$ sides is given by the formula $(n-2) \\times 180\u00b0$.\n\nFor a hexagon, $n = 6$:\n$(6-2) \\times 180\u00b0 = 4 \\times 180\u00b0 = 720\u00b0$\n\nAnswer: 720", "correct": true, "gold": "720"}
{"qid": "tq:qb_2546", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "The sum of the interior angles of any simple polygon with \\(n\\) sides is given by the formula \\((n-2) \\times 180^\\circ\\).\n\nA hexagon has \\(n=6\\) sides, so the sum is \\((6-2) \\times 180^\\circ = 720^\\circ\\).\n\n(This holds for any convex or simple concave hexagon; a regular hexagon has six equal interior angles of \\(120^\\circ\\) each.)\n\nAnswer: 720", "correct": true, "gold": "720"}
