{"qid": "tq:odql_4800", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "openai/gpt-5.4", "resp": "The Winter Olympics have been hosted outside Europe by the United States, Canada, Japan, and South Korea. Of those, only **South Korea** has hosted them exactly once: **Pyeongchang 2018**.\n\nAnswer: South Korea", "correct": false, "gold": "CANADA (1988)"}
{"qid": "tq:sfq_2368", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "The Gestapo (Geheime Staatspolizei) was created in 1933 under Hermann G\u00f6ring\u2019s Prussian interior ministry, with Rudolf Diels as its first chief. In April 1934 Heinrich Himmler, already Reichsf\u00fchrer-SS, assumed control of the Prussian Gestapo and placed it under SS authority; Reinhard Heydrich became its operational director.  \n\nOn 17 June 1936 Hitler formally appointed Himmler Chief of German Police (Chef der Deutschen Polizei). This decree unified all state and national police forces\u2014including the Gestapo\u2014under a single SS-controlled command. From that date onward Himmler held the legal and administrative headship of the Gestapo, while Heydrich (and later Heinrich M\u00fcller) exercised day-to-day direction within the Security Police (SiPo) apparatus.  \n\nThus the individual who was head of the Gestapo from 1936 is Heinrich Himmler.\n\nAnswer: Heinrich Himmler", "correct": true, "gold": "Heinrich Himmler"}
{"qid": "tq:odql_4800", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5", "resp": "**China** is the only non-European country to have hosted the Winter Olympics only once (Beijing 2022).\n\nOther non-European hosts have hosted multiple times:\n- **USA**: Lake Placid (1932, 1980), Squaw Valley (1960), Salt Lake City (2002)\n- **Canada**: Calgary (1988), Vancouver (2010)\n- **Japan**: Sapporo (1972), Nagano (1998)\n\nAnswer: China", "correct": false, "gold": "CANADA (1988)"}
{"qid": "tq:bt_2785", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "MAI-Thinking-1", "resp": "The term \"axe\" is most commonly used as slang for a **guitar**. \r\n\r\nThis originated in jazz and blues culture and became especially popular in rock music, often used to refer to an electric guitar. \r\n\r\nAnswer: Guitar", "correct": true, "gold": "Guitar"}
{"qid": "tq:qb_2546", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "MAI-Thinking-1", "resp": "A hexagon has 6 sides. Using the formula for the sum of interior angles of a polygon: **(n - 2) \u00d7 180\u00b0**, where n is the number of sides, we get **(6 - 2) \u00d7 180\u00b0 = 4 \u00d7 180\u00b0 = 720\u00b0**. \r\n\r\nAnswer: 720\u00b0", "correct": true, "gold": "720"}
{"qid": "tq:odql_9880", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "openai/gpt-5.4", "resp": "In Greek mythology, the virgin goddess of the hearth, home, and cooking who gave up her seat among the Twelve Olympians for Dionysus was **Hestia**.\n\nAnswer: Hestia", "correct": true, "gold": "HESTIA"}
{"qid": "tq:odql_9880", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5", "resp": "Hestia gave up her Olympian seat to Dionysus while she tended to the sacred fire on Mount Olympus.\n\nAnswer: Hestia", "correct": true, "gold": "HESTIA"}
{"qid": "tq:odql_9880", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "Hestia is one of the six original Olympians (the children of Cronus and Rhea) and the virgin goddess specifically associated with the hearth, domestic life, and the sacred fire. Ancient sources record that the Olympian circle was limited to twelve seats; when Dionysus ascended and claimed a place among them, Hestia voluntarily relinquished her throne so that he could be included, thereafter devoting herself entirely to tending the eternal flame on Olympus. This episode is attested in later mythographic traditions that reconcile the varying lists of the Twelve Olympians. No other virgin goddess matches the description.\n\nAnswer: Hestia", "correct": true, "gold": "HESTIA"}
{"qid": "tq:odql_9880", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "DeepSeek-V4-Flash", "resp": "The goddess described is Hestia. She gave up her seat among the Twelve Olympians to Dionysus to tend the sacred flame.\n\nAnswer: Hestia", "correct": true, "gold": "HESTIA"}
{"qid": "tq:odql_9880", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "The goddess is **Hestia**, daughter of Cronus and Rhea. As the peaceful virgin goddess of the hearth and domestic life, she voluntarily relinquished her position among the Twelve Olympians to Dionysus to avoid conflict among the gods, choosing instead to tend the sacred eternal flame on Mount Olympus.\n\nAnswer: Hestia", "correct": true, "gold": "HESTIA"}
