{"qid": "tq:odql_4800", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "The Winter Olympics have been hosted a total of 24 times through 2022. The complete list of host countries and their frequencies is:\n- United States: 4\n- France: 3\n- Italy: 2 (plus one future)\n- Austria: 2\n- Switzerland: 2\n- Japan: 2\n- Norway: 2\n- Canada: 2\n- Germany: 1\n- Yugoslavia: 1\n- Russia: 1\n- South Korea: 1\n- China: 1\nRussia is conventionally grouped with Europe (its population, capital, and Olympic governance structures are overwhelmingly European, and Sochi lies entirely in Europe). This leaves only five non-European host countries: the United States, Canada, Japan, South Korea, and China.\nOf those five, the United States, Canada, and Japan have each hosted more than once. South Korea has therefore been the sole non-European nation whose single hosting (Pyeongchang 2018) satisfies the \u201conly once\u201d criterion. (China\u2019s later hosting in 2022 does not alter the logic if the question predates that Games.)\nAnswer: South Korea", "correct": false, "gold": "CANADA (1988)"}
