{"qid": "tq:qw_16174", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "A common feature of these three animals is **parthenogenesis** (asexual reproduction where females produce offspring without mating).\n\nKomodo dragons, aphids, and whiptail lizards are all capable of reproducing through \"virgin birth\"\u2014producing viable offspring from unfertilized eggs. This is particularly notable in whiptail lizards, where entire species consist only of females; in aphids, which alternate between sexual and asexual reproduction; and in Komodo dragons, where isolated females can still reproduce.\n\nAnswer: They can all reproduce asexually through parthenogenesis (producing offspring without mating).", "correct": false, "gold": "The ability to reproduce asexually"}
