{"qid": "tq:dpql_2272", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5", "resp": "In heraldry, \"trippant\" describes an animal (typically a deer, stag, or similar creature) depicted as walking gracefully, with one foot raised as if in motion.\n\nAnswer: Walking (specifically, walking gracefully with one foot raised, as commonly depicted for deer or stags in heraldry)", "correct": false, "gold": "Running"}
{"qid": "tq:tb_343", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "DeepSeek-V4-Flash", "resp": "Ida Tarbell is known for her expose of the corrupt practices of the Standard Oil Company.\n\nAnswer: Standard Oil", "correct": true, "gold": "Standard Oil"}
{"qid": "tq:dpql_2272", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "In heraldry, \"trippant\" is an attitude (posture) used specifically for stags, deer, or similar beasts of the chase. It shows the animal in profile, moving forward with the right foreleg raised and the others on the ground\u2014equivalent to the more general term \"passant\" but implying a light, lively gait.\nAnswer: walking/trotting (right foreleg raised)", "correct": false, "gold": "Running"}
