{"qid": "tq:tb_343", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "Cohere-command-a-plus-05-2026", "resp": "<|START_TEXT|>Ida\u202fTarbell\u2019s 1904 investigative work, *The History of the Standard Oil Company*, exposed the monopolistic and unethical business tactics of Standard Oil, making it the target of her famous expos\u00e9. John\u202fD.\u202fRockefeller, who founded Standard Oil, was indeed a prominent figure associated with the company and likely resented her revelations.\n\n**Answer:** Standard Oil.<|END_TEXT|>", "correct": true, "gold": "Standard Oil"}
{"qid": "tq:tb_343", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "Ida Tarbell is best known for her groundbreaking expos\u00e9 \"The History of the Standard Oil Company,\" which detailed the monopolistic and corrupt business practices of **Standard Oil**. Her investigative work, published in the early 1900s, helped expose how the company used unfair tactics to crush competitors and control the oil industry, ultimately contributing to the government's antitrust case that broke up the monopoly in 1911.\n\nAnswer: Standard Oil (or Standard Oil Company)", "correct": true, "gold": "Standard Oil"}
