{"qid": "tq:tb_343", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "Ida Tarbell was a leading \"muckraker\" investigative journalist of the Progressive Era. Her landmark 19-part series (later published as the book *The History of the Standard Oil Company*) meticulously documented the monopolistic, predatory, and often illegal tactics used by John D. Rockefeller\u2019s Standard Oil trust to crush competitors and dominate the petroleum industry. The work helped fuel public outrage and ultimately contributed to the U.S. Supreme Court\u2019s 1911 decision to break up the company.\n\nAnswer: Standard Oil (Company)", "correct": true, "gold": "Standard Oil"}
