{"qid": "tq:odql_12783", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "The 1968 musical film *Chitty Chitty Bang Bang* opens with the title vehicle as a neglected, broken-down racing car stored at a rural garage. Its owner, the elderly Mr. Coggins, is about to sell it for scrap when the eccentric inventor Caractacus Potts offers him a modest sum. Potts then tows the chassis home and, with the help of his two children, completely restores and modifies it\u2014installing the famous fold-out wings, flotation devices, and other gadgets that give the car its magical abilities.\n\nThus the purchaser and rebuilder is unambiguously Caractacus Potts.\n\nAnswer: Caractacus Potts", "correct": true, "gold": "Caractacus Potts"}
