{"qid": "tq:dpql_4756", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "openai/gpt-5.4", "resp": "\u201cVinegar Joe\u201d was General Joseph Stilwell, a senior U.S. Army commander in the China-Burma-India theater during World War II.\n\nAnswer: General Joseph Stilwell", "correct": true, "gold": "Stillwell"}
{"qid": "tq:dpql_4756", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "The nickname \"Vinegar Joe\" referred to **General Joseph Stilwell** (1883-1946), who commanded U.S. forces in the China-Burma-India Theater during World War II. He earned the moniker due to his caustic personality, blunt criticism of allies (particularly Chiang Kai-shek), and generally abrasive demeanor.\n\nAnswer: Joseph Stilwell", "correct": true, "gold": "Stillwell"}
