{"qid": "tq:qg_3854", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "The nickname \"Old Ironsides\" has long been attached to one specific vessel: the wooden-hulled, three-masted heavy frigate launched at Boston on 21 October 1797. That ship\u2019s official designation, both at the time of her launch and ever since, is USS Constitution (or, more formally, United States Ship Constitution). No other commissioned U.S. Navy warship bears that name or that historic nickname.\nAnswer: USS Constitution", "correct": true, "gold": "USS Constitution"}
