{"qid": "tq:odql_11414", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "In 1907, at age 35\u201336, Synge was living mainly in Dublin while battling Hodgkin\u2019s disease. His masterpiece *The Playboy of the Western World* opened at the Abbey Theatre on 26 January; the play\u2019s irreverent tone and use of the word \u201cshift\u201d provoked nightly riots that lasted a week, requiring police protection for the cast. He continued revising the text, corresponded with his fianc\u00e9e Molly Allgood, and made a brief trip to the Aran Islands for further material before the year closed.\n\nAnswer: 1907 \u2013 Playboy riots at the Abbey, ongoing illness, and work with Molly Allgood.", "correct": false, "gold": "1871-1909"}
