{"qid": "tq:qb_2071", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "Sherlock Holmes, the fictional detective created by Arthur Conan Doyle, is frequently described in the canon as having eccentric and untidy habits in his Baker Street rooms. One recurring detail is that he stored his pipe tobacco inside a Persian slipper (often hung near the fireplace), using the toe of the slipper as a convenient pouch. This is mentioned across multiple stories and is distinct from other quirky storage choices such as unanswered correspondence pinned to the mantel or cigars kept in the coal-scuttle.\nAnswer: tobacco (pipe tobacco)", "correct": true, "gold": "Tobacco"}
