{"qid": "tq:sfq_25538", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "The British Victorian writer was **George Eliot** (the pen name of Mary Ann Evans). She began living with the philosopher and critic George Henry Lewes in 1854. Since Lewes was unable to obtain a divorce from his estranged wife, they could not marry, but they lived together as husband and wife until Lewes's death in 1878\u2014a partnership of 24 years.\n\nAnswer: George Eliot (Mary Ann Evans)", "correct": true, "gold": "GEORGE ELIOT"}
