{"qid": "tq:sfq_18204", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "The painting *A Dance to the Music of Time* (c. 1634\u20131636) in the Wallace Collection is by the French Baroque artist **Nicolas Poussin**. The work depicts four figures representing the seasons or ages of man dancing in a circle while the figure of Time plays music on a lyre.\n\nAnswer: Nicolas Poussin", "correct": true, "gold": "Nicholas Poussin"}
{"qid": "tq:sfq_18204", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "The painting in question is a well-known work from the Baroque period, created for Cardinal Giulio Rospigliosi (later Pope Clement IX). Its subject draws on classical mythology and the theme of the four seasons dancing in a circle to Time's music, a motif that aligns precisely with the style, composition, and documented chronology of Nicolas Poussin's output in Rome during the mid-1630s. No other artist of the period produced a work matching this title, date range, and current location in the Wallace Collection.\nAnswer: Nicolas Poussin", "correct": true, "gold": "Nicholas Poussin"}
