{"qid": "tq:qb_6822", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "Steamboat Willie (1928) was the first Mickey Mouse short to be publicly released and distributed, with synchronized sound. Although two earlier shorts (Plane Crazy and The Gallopin' Gaucho) were produced beforehand, they were not released until after Steamboat Willie and are therefore not regarded as the debut.\n\nAnswer: Steamboat Willie", "correct": true, "gold": "Steamboat Willie"}
{"qid": "tq:qb_6822", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5", "resp": "Mickey Mouse first appeared in \"Plane Crazy,\" but it wasn't released until after \"Steamboat Willie,\" which premiered first (November 18, 1928) and is officially recognized as his debut film.\n\nAnswer: Steamboat Willie", "correct": true, "gold": "Steamboat Willie"}
{"qid": "tq:qb_6822", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "Cohere-command-a-plus-05-2026", "resp": "<|START_TEXT|>Mickey Mouse first appeared publicly in a released animated short; while he was created earlier, his official debut film that introduced him to audiences worldwide is the 1928 cartoon \"Steamboat Willie.\"  \nAnswer: Steamboat Willie<|END_TEXT|>", "correct": true, "gold": "Steamboat Willie"}
{"qid": "tq:jp_4324", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "The standard Monopoly board consists of 40 squares arranged in a loop, with Go at position 0. The four corner squares are therefore spaced exactly 10 positions apart:\n- Position 0: Go\n- Position 10: Jail\n- Position 20: Free Parking\n- Position 30: Go to Jail\nBecause the board is square, the geometrically opposite corner from Go is Free Parking (20 steps away). In Euclidean terms the centers of these two corner squares are also farther apart than the center of any intervening side square is from Go, confirming that Free Parking is the unique farthest square.\nAnswer: Free Parking", "correct": true, "gold": "Free Parking"}
