{"qid": "tq:tb_960", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "The hint identifies a major global city that hosted the 2014 FIFA World Cup and the 2016 Summer Olympics; that city is Rio de Janeiro.  \n\nThe relevant Simpsons episode is the season-13 installment \u201cBlame It on Lisa\u201d (first broadcast March 2002). In it the family travels to Rio, and the city is depicted as crime-ridden and chaotic. One scene shows Bart being menaced (and briefly endangered) by a large boa constrictor.  \n\nRio\u2019s municipal tourism board (RioTur) publicly denounced the portrayal as defamatory and announced it was considering legal action against Fox, exactly as the question states.  \n\nThus the city whose tourism department issued the threat is Rio de Janeiro.\n\nAnswer: Rio de Janeiro", "correct": true, "gold": "Rio"}
