{"qid": "tq:qb_5139", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "Saddam Hussein replaced Ahmed Hassan al-Bakr as President of Iraq on July 16, 1979, after al-Bakr resigned citing health reasons. Saddam, who had been the country's de facto leader for several years as Vice Chairman of the Revolutionary Command Council and Vice President, formally seized power and immediately consolidated his rule by purging rivals.\n\nAnswer: Saddam Hussein", "correct": true, "gold": "Saddam Hussein"}
