{"qid": "tq:odql_10748", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "Looking at Virginia Wade's career Grand Slam women's doubles titles, she won exactly 4 major doubles championships:\n\n1. **1973 Australian Open** \u2013 with Margaret Court\n2. **1973 French Open** \u2013 with Margaret Court  \n3. **1973 US Open** \u2013 with Margaret Court\n4. **1975 US Open** \u2013 with Margaret Court\n\nAll four titles were won with the same Australian partner. Margaret Court (n\u00e9e Smith) was the dominant Australian player of that era, and she and Wade formed a successful partnership, winning three majors together in 1973 and the US Open again in 1975. Wade never won the women's doubles at Wimbledon (though she did win the mixed doubles there in 1973 and 1977).\n\nAnswer: Margaret Court", "correct": true, "gold": "MARGARET COURT"}
{"qid": "tq:dpql_475", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5", "resp": "Agricultural lime's active ingredient is calcium carbonate (CaCO\u2083), often combined with magnesium carbonate (MgCO\u2083) in dolomitic lime varieties.\n\nAnswer: Calcium carbonate (CaCO\u2083)", "correct": true, "gold": "CALCIUM CARBONATE"}
