{"qid": "tq:dpql_475", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "Agricultural lime (or aglime) is a soil amendment used to neutralize acidity. It consists primarily of pulverized limestone or chalk, whose key reactive component is the mineral calcite.\nThis means the active chemical compound is calcium carbonate (\\(\\mathrm{CaCO_3}\\)).\nAnswer: calcium carbonate (CaCO\u2083)", "correct": true, "gold": "CALCIUM CARBONATE"}
