{"qid": "tq:sfq_17649", "domain": "triviaqa", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "The Manchester Ship Canal opened in 1894 and included a complex of docks along its length. On the stretch that later became Salford Quays, five separate basins were constructed and collectively named the Pomona Docks. Pomona is the Roman goddess of fruit trees, orchards and gardens; the name was chosen because the surrounding land had historically been used for market gardens and orchards.  \n\nThe same name was later given to the Metrolink stop (Pomona station) that now serves the redeveloped area, confirming the identity of the goddess.  \n\nAnswer: Pomona", "correct": true, "gold": "Pomona"}
