{"qid": "gsm:5", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "openai/gpt-5.4", "resp": "Let \\(r\\) be the number of rats in each of the 3 cages.\n\n- Rats: \\(3r\\) rats total, each gets 6 pieces of straw  \n  \\(\\Rightarrow 3r \\cdot 6 = 18r\\)\n\n- Hamsters: 10 cages, 1 hamster per cage, each gets 5 pieces  \n  \\(\\Rightarrow 10 \\cdot 5 = 50\\)\n\n- Rabbits: 20 pieces total\n\nTotal straw distributed:\n\\[\n18r + 50 + 20 = 160\n\\]\n\n\\[\n18r + 70 = 160\n\\]\n\n\\[\n18r = 90\n\\]\n\n\\[\nr = 5\n\\]\n\nAnswer: 5", "correct": true, "gold": "5"}
{"qid": "gsm:4", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "DeepSeek-V4-Flash", "resp": "We know Jay builds 20 snowballs per hour, which is 20 snowballs in 60 minutes, so he builds at a rate of 1 snowball every 3 minutes.  \nEvery 15 minutes, 2 snowballs melt. That means in 15 minutes, he builds 5 snowballs (since 15 \u00f7 3 = 5) but loses 2, for a net gain of 3 snowballs every 15 minutes.  \n\nTo get 60 snowballs, we need to find how many 15-minute intervals are needed:  \n60 \u00f7 3 = 20 intervals.  \n20 intervals \u00d7 15 minutes = 300 minutes, which is 5 hours.\n\nBut we should check if the melting happens at the end of each 15-minute period, and if the final count is exactly 60 at that moment. After 20 intervals, net gain is 60, so yes.\n\nAnswer: 5 hours", "correct": true, "gold": "5"}
{"qid": "gsm:4", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Cohere-command-a-plus-05-2026", "resp": "<|START_TEXT|>To find the time needed, determine the net rate at which the number of snowballs increases.\n\n- Building rate: 20 snowballs per hour \u2192 \\( \\frac{20}{4}=5 \\) snowballs every 15 minutes.\n- Melting rate: 2 snowballs every 15 minutes.\n\nNet gain per 15\u2011minute interval:  \n\\(5 \\text{ (built)} - 2 \\text{ (melted)} = 3\\) snowballs.\n\nTo accumulate 60 snowballs:\n\\[\n\\frac{60\\ \\text{snowballs}}{3\\ \\text{snowballs per 15 min}} = 20 \\text{ intervals of 15 minutes}\n\\]\n\nTotal time:\n\\[\n20 \\times 15\\ \\text{minutes} = 300\\ \\text{minutes} = 5\\ \\text{hours}\n\\]\n\nAnswer: 5 hours.<|END_TEXT|>", "correct": true, "gold": "5"}
{"qid": "gsm:5", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "DeepSeek-V4-Flash", "resp": "We are told:\n\n- Rats: 3 cages, equal groups, each rat gets 6 pieces.\n- Hamsters: 10 cages, each alone, each gets 5 pieces \u2192 10 \u00d7 5 = 50 pieces.\n- Rabbits: 20 pieces total.\n- Total straw used: 160 pieces.\n\nFirst, find straw used for rats:  \nTotal straw = rat straw + hamster straw + rabbit straw  \n160 = rat straw + 50 + 20  \nRat straw = 160 \u2212 70 = 90 pieces.\n\nEach rat gets 6 pieces, so number of rats = 90 \u00f7 6 = 15 rats.\n\nThese 15 rats are in 3 cages equally, so per cage: 15 \u00f7 3 = 5 rats.\n\nAnswer: 5", "correct": true, "gold": "5"}
