{"qid": "gsm:5", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "MAI-Thinking-1", "resp": "Let $r$ be the number of rats in each cage. \r\n\r\n- **Rats:** 3 cages \u00d7 $r$ rats \u00d7 6 pieces = $18r$ pieces\r\n- **Hamsters:** 10 cages \u00d7 1 hamster \u00d7 5 pieces = 50 pieces\r\n- **Rabbits:** 20 pieces\r\n\r\nTotal straw: $18r + 50 + 20 = 18r + 70 = 160$. \r\n\r\nSolve: $18r = 90 \\implies r = 5$. \r\n\r\nAnswer: 5", "correct": true, "gold": "5"}
{"qid": "gsm:7", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "openai/gpt-5.4", "resp": "4 horses \u00d7 5 lb per meal = 20 lb per meal total.\n\nHe feeds them twice a day:\n20 \u00d7 2 = 40 lb per day.\n\nFor 5 days:\n40 \u00d7 5 = 200 lb total oats.\n\nEach bag is 50 lb:\n200 \u00f7 50 = 4 bags.\n\nAnswer: 4 bags", "correct": true, "gold": "4"}
{"qid": "gsm:6", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Cohere-command-a-plus-05-2026", "resp": "<|START_TEXT|>First, determine the number of articles written each day.\n\n- Monday: 5 articles  \n- Tuesday: \u201c2/5 times more\u201d than Monday means she wrote the original 5 articles plus an additional \\( \\frac{2}{5} \\times 5 = 2 \\) articles.  \n  So, Tuesday = \\(5 + 2 = 7\\) articles.  \n- Wednesday: twice the Tuesday amount \u2192 \\(2 \\times 7 = 14\\) articles.\n\nTotal articles over the three days:  \n\\(5 + 7 + 14 = 26\\) articles.\n\nEach article takes 4 hours to complete, so total hours spent:  \n\\(26 \\times 4 = 104\\) hours.\n\nAnswer: 104<|END_TEXT|>", "correct": true, "gold": "104"}
{"qid": "gsm:7", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5", "resp": "**Answer: 4 bags**\n\nCalculation:\n- Each horse eats 5 lbs per meal \u00d7 2 meals/day = 10 lbs per horse per day\n- 4 horses \u00d7 10 lbs = 40 lbs per day for all horses\n- 40 lbs/day \u00d7 5 days = 200 lbs total needed\n- 200 lbs \u00f7 50 lbs/bag = 4 bags\n\nAnswer: 4", "correct": true, "gold": "4"}
