{"qid": "gsm:6", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "Here's the step-by-step calculation:\n\n**Monday:** She wrote 5 articles.\n\n**Tuesday:** She wrote $\\frac{2}{5}$ times the number of articles from Monday (interpreting \"2/5 times more\" as $\\frac{2}{5}$ of Monday's total, since the alternative interpretation would require working over 24 hours per day, which is impossible).\n$$\\frac{2}{5} \\times 5 = 2 \\text{ articles}$$\n\n**Wednesday:** She wrote twice the number of articles from Tuesday.\n$$2 \\times 2 = 4 \\text{ articles}$$\n\n**Total articles:** $5 + 2 + 4 = 11$ articles\n\n**Total hours:** Since each article takes 4 hours:\n$$11 \\times 4 = 44 \\text{ hours}$$\n\nAnswer: 44", "correct": false, "gold": "104"}
{"qid": "gsm:9", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "openai/gpt-5.4", "resp": "Let the smallest angle be \\(x\\).\n\nThen the other two angles are:\n- \\(2x\\)\n- \\(3x\\)\n\nSince angles in a triangle sum to 180\u00b0:\n\\[\nx + 2x + 3x = 180\n\\]\n\\[\n6x = 180\n\\]\n\\[\nx = 30\n\\]\n\nSo the angles are:\n- \\(30^\\circ\\)\n- \\(60^\\circ\\)\n- \\(90^\\circ\\)\n\nThe largest angle is \\(90^\\circ\\).\n\nAnswer: 90", "correct": true, "gold": "90"}
{"qid": "gsm:9", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "DeepSeek-V4-Flash", "resp": "We are told the three angles add to 180\u00b0.  \nLet the smallest angle be \\( x \\).  \nThen the other two angles are \\( 2x \\) and \\( 3x \\).  \n\nThe sum is:  \n\\[\nx + 2x + 3x = 180\n\\]  \n\\[\n6x = 180\n\\]  \n\\[\nx = 30\n\\]  \n\nThe angles are \\( 30^\\circ \\), \\( 60^\\circ \\), and \\( 90^\\circ \\).  \nThe largest angle is \\( 90^\\circ \\).  \n\nAnswer: 90", "correct": true, "gold": "90"}
