{"qid": "gsm:9", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "Let $x$ be the measure of the smallest angle in degrees.\n\nThe three angles are:\n- Smallest angle: $x$\n- Second angle: $2x$ (twice the smallest)\n- Third angle: $3x$ (three times the smallest)\n\nSince the angles in a triangle sum to $180\u00b0$:\n$$x + 2x + 3x = 180$$\n$$6x = 180$$\n$$x = 30$$\n\nThe angles are $30\u00b0$, $60\u00b0$, and $90\u00b0$.\n\nThe largest angle is $3x = 3(30) = 90\u00b0$.\n\nAnswer: 90", "correct": true, "gold": "90"}
{"qid": "gsm:5", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "The total amount of straw distributed is 160 pieces. This covers the rats, hamsters, and rabbits.\nThe rabbits receive 20 pieces in total, and there are 10 hamsters (one per cage, as they are kept alone) receiving 5 pieces each. This accounts for \\(20 + 50 = 70\\) pieces.\nThe remaining straw is therefore \\(160 - 70 = 90\\) pieces, all of which goes to the rats.\nEach rat receives 6 pieces of straw, so the total number of rats is \\(90 / 6 = 15\\).\nThese 15 rats are divided equally across 3 cages, so the number of rats per cage is \\(15 / 3 = 5\\).\nAnswer: 5", "correct": true, "gold": "5"}
{"qid": "gsm:10", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "openai/gpt-5.4", "resp": "Each flower is 12 inches wide, which is 1 foot.\n\nIf Pat places \\(n\\) flowers, they take up:\n- \\(n\\) feet for the flowers\n- \\(1.5(n-1)\\) feet for the spaces between them\n\nSo the total length is:\n\\[\nn + 1.5(n-1) = 111\n\\]\n\nSolve:\n\\[\nn + 1.5n - 1.5 = 111\n\\]\n\\[\n2.5n = 112.5\n\\]\n\\[\nn = 45\n\\]\n\nPat needs 45 flowers total.\n\nShe already has 17, so she must buy:\n\\[\n45 - 17 = 28\n\\]\n\nAt \\$6 each:\n\\[\n28 \\times 6 = 168\n\\]\n\nAnswer: $168", "correct": false, "gold": "342"}
{"qid": "gsm:8", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "MAI-Thinking-1", "resp": "Digimon's 20th anniversary means it came out **20 years ago**. \r\n\r\n- John's age now = 28, so his age when it came out = 28 - 20 = **8 years old**.\r\n- At that time, John was twice as old as Jim, so Jim's age then = 8 \u00f7 2 = **4 years old**.\r\n- Now, Jim's age = 4 + 20 = **24 years old**.\r\n\r\nAnswer: Jim is 24 years old.", "correct": true, "gold": "24"}
{"qid": "gsm:10", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "DeepSeek-V4-Flash", "resp": "We need to figure out how many plants fit in 111 feet, given each plant is 12 inches (1 foot) wide and needs 1.5 feet spacing between plants.\n\nFirst, think of the arrangement:  \nIf you have one plant, it takes up 1 foot of width.  \nBetween plants, you need 1.5 feet.  \nSo for *n* plants, the total length used is:  \n1 foot (first plant) + (n - 1) * (1.5 + 1) feet?  \nActually careful:  \n- Plant width = 1 foot  \n- Gap between plants = 1.5 feet  \n\nSo for n plants, the total length = 1 (first plant) + (n-1)*(1 + 1.5) = 1 + (n-1)*2.5.\n\nSet that equal to 111:  \n1 + (n-1)*2.5 = 111  \n(n-1)*2.5 = 110  \nn-1 = 44  \nn = 45 plants total.\n\nPat already has 17, so she needs 45 - 17 = 28 more plants.  \nEach costs $6, so cost = 28 * 6 = $168.\n\nAnswer: $168", "correct": false, "gold": "342"}
