{"qid": "gsm:10", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Cohere-command-a-plus-05-2026", "resp": "<|START_TEXT|>To determine how many additional plants Pat needs, first calculate the maximum number of plants that can fit in the 111\u2011foot bed.\n\nEach plant occupies 1\u202fft, and there must be a 1.5\u202fft gap between consecutive plants. For \\(N\\) plants:\n\\[\n\\text{Total length} = N \\times 1\\text{ ft} + (N-1) \\times 1.5\\text{ ft}\n\\]\nSet this \u2264\u202f111\u202fft:\n\\[\nN + 1.5(N-1) \\le 111 \\\\\n2.5N - 1.5 \\le 111 \\\\\n2.5N \\le 112.5 \\\\\nN \\le 45\n\\]\n\nSo at most 45 plants can be placed. Pat already has 17, so she needs:\n\\[\n45 - 17 = 28 \\text{ more plants}\n\\]\n\nEach new plant costs \\$6, thus the total cost is:\n\\[\n28 \\times \\$6 = \\$168\n\\]\n\nAnswer: $168<|END_TEXT|>", "correct": false, "gold": "342"}
