{"qid": "gsm:9", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "The three angles can be denoted as \\(x\\), \\(2x\\), and \\(3x\\), where \\(x\\) is the smallest angle. These must sum to \\(180^\\circ\\):\n\\[\nx + 2x + 3x = 180^\\circ\n\\]\n\\[\n6x = 180^\\circ\n\\]\n\\[\nx = 30^\\circ\n\\]\nThe angles are therefore \\(30^\\circ\\), \\(60^\\circ\\), and \\(90^\\circ\\). The largest is \\(3x = 90^\\circ\\).\nThis is the only valid assignment, as the largest angle must be the one equal to \\(3x\\) (any other pairing would violate the ordering or the triangle angle sum).\nAnswer: 90", "correct": true, "gold": "90"}
