{"qid": "gsm:10", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "The flower bed is 111 feet long. Each plant is 1 foot wide (12 inches) and requires an additional 1.5 feet of spacing between plants. This means the first plant occupies 1 foot and each additional plant occupies 2.5 feet.\nSolving \\(1 + 2.5(n-1) = 111\\) yields exactly 45 plants to fill the bed. After subtracting the 17 plants already owned, 28 plants must be purchased at $6 each.\n\\(28 \\times 6 = 168\\)\nAnswer: 168", "correct": false, "gold": "342"}
