{"qid": "gsm:20", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "openai/gpt-5.4", "resp": "Five lollipops cost:\n\\(5 \\times \\$0.40 = \\$2.00\\)\n\nSo the four candies cost:\n\\(\\$3.20 - \\$2.00 = \\$1.20\\)\n\nEach candy costs:\n\\(\\$1.20 \\div 4 = \\$0.30\\)\n\nNow find the cost of 10 lollipops and 10 candies:\n- 10 lollipops: \\(10 \\times \\$0.40 = \\$4.00\\)\n- 10 candies: \\(10 \\times \\$0.30 = \\$3.00\\)\n\nTotal:\n\\(\\$4.00 + \\$3.00 = \\$7.00\\)\n\nAnswer: $7.00", "correct": true, "gold": "7"}
{"qid": "gsm:20", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "DeepSeek-V4-Flash", "resp": "Let\u2019s break it down step by step.\n\nManolo bought 5 lollipops at $0.40 each:  \n5 \u00d7 0.40 = $2.00 spent on lollipops.\n\nTotal cost was $3.20, so the cost of the 4 candies is:  \n3.20 \u2212 2.00 = $1.20.\n\nCost per candy:  \n1.20 \u00f7 4 = $0.30.\n\nNow, 10 lollipops cost:  \n10 \u00d7 0.40 = $4.00.\n\n10 candies cost:  \n10 \u00d7 0.30 = $3.00.\n\nTotal for 10 lollipops and 10 candies:  \n4.00 + 3.00 = $7.00.\n\nAnswer: $7.00", "correct": true, "gold": "7"}
{"qid": "gsm:20", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "First, find the cost of the candies. Five lollipops cost $5 \\times \\$0.40 = \\$2.00$. Since the total was $\\$3.20$, the four candies cost $\\$3.20 - \\$2.00 = \\$1.20$. Thus, one candy costs $\\$1.20 \\div 4 = \\$0.30$.\n\nNow calculate the new total: Ten lollipops cost $10 \\times \\$0.40 = \\$4.00$, and ten candies cost $10 \\times \\$0.30 = \\$3.00$. The total is $\\$4.00 + \\$3.00 = \\$7.00$.\n\nAnswer: $7.00 (or $7)", "correct": true, "gold": "7"}
{"qid": "gsm:20", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5", "resp": "**Finding the cost of one candy:**\n\n- 5 lollipops cost: 5 \u00d7 $0.40 = $2.00\n- Since 5 lollipops + 4 candies = $3.20\n- 4 candies cost: $3.20 - $2.00 = $1.20\n- 1 candy costs: $1.20 \u00f7 4 = $0.30\n\n**Finding the cost of 10 lollipops and 10 candies:**\n\n- 10 lollipops: 10 \u00d7 $0.40 = $4.00\n- 10 candies: 10 \u00d7 $0.30 = $3.00\n- Total: $4.00 + $3.00 = $7.00\n\nAnswer: $7.00", "correct": true, "gold": "7"}
{"qid": "gsm:19", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "MAI-Thinking-1", "resp": "**Reasoning:** \r\n\r\n1. **Potatoes:** Daisy bought a bag of potatoes that weighed 5 pounds. \r\n2. **Sweet Potatoes:** The bag of sweet potatoes weighed 2 times as much as the potatoes. So, 2 \u00d7 5 = 10 pounds.\r\n3. **Carrots:** The bag of carrots weighed 3 pounds fewer than the sweet potatoes. So, 10 - 3 = 7 pounds. \r\n\r\nAnswer: 7 pounds", "correct": true, "gold": "7"}
{"qid": "gsm:20", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "Five lollipops cost \\(5 \\times 0.40 = 2.00\\). Subtracting from the given total leaves \\(3.20 - 2.00 = 1.20\\) for four candies, or \\(1.20 / 4 = 0.30\\) each.  \nTen lollipops therefore cost \\(10 \\times 0.40 = 4.00\\) and ten candies cost \\(10 \\times 0.30 = 3.00\\), for a combined total of \\(7.00\\).\nAnswer: $7.00", "correct": true, "gold": "7"}
{"qid": "gsm:21", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "openai/gpt-5.4", "resp": "Each pair of glasses costs:\n- first glass: $5\n- second glass: 60% of $5 = $3\n\nSo every 2 glasses cost $8.\n\nKylar buys 16 glasses, which is 8 pairs:\n- 8 \u00d7 $8 = $64\n\nAnswer: $64", "correct": true, "gold": "64"}
{"qid": "gsm:21", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "DeepSeek-V4-Flash", "resp": "Let\u2019s break it down:\n\n- The first glass costs $5.  \n- The second glass costs 60% of $5 = $3.  \n- This pattern repeats: odd-numbered glasses cost $5, even-numbered glasses cost $3.\n\nFor 16 glasses, there are 8 odd-numbered and 8 even-numbered glasses.\n\nCost = \\( 8 \\times 5 + 8 \\times 3 = 40 + 24 = 64 \\).\n\nAnswer: $64", "correct": true, "gold": "64"}
{"qid": "gsm:20", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Cohere-command-a-plus-05-2026", "resp": "<|START_TEXT|>First, determine the cost of one candy.  \n- Total cost for 5 lollipops and 4 candies = $3.20.  \n- Cost of 5 lollipops = 5 \u00d7 $0.40 = $2.00.  \n- Remaining amount for 4 candies = $3.20 \u2212 $2.00 = $1.20.  \n- Cost per candy = $1.20 \u00f7 4 = $0.30.\n\nNow calculate the cost of 10 lollipops and 10 candies:  \n- Cost of 10 lollipops = 10 \u00d7 $0.40 = $4.00.  \n- Cost of 10 candies = 10 \u00d7 $0.30 = $3.00.  \n- Total cost = $4.00 + $3.00 = $7.00.\n\nAnswer: $7.00<|END_TEXT|>", "correct": true, "gold": "7"}
{"qid": "gsm:21", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "The pricing alternates between full price ($5) and the discounted price (60% of $5 = $3).\n\nFor 16 glasses:\n- 8 glasses at $5 each = $40\n- 8 glasses at $3 each = $24\n\nTotal: $40 + $24 = $64\n\nAnswer: $64", "correct": true, "gold": "64"}
