{"qid": "gsm:22", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "DeepSeek-V4-Flash", "resp": "Let's break it down step by step.\n\n- Total bikes sold: 300  \n- Trekking bikes: half of 300 = 150  \n- BMX bikes: 15% of 300 = 0.15 \u00d7 300 = 45  \n- MTB bikes: the rest = 300 \u2212 (150 + 45) = 105  \n\nPrices:  \n- MTB: $500  \n- BMX: half of $500 = $250  \n- Trekking: $450  \n\nEarnings:  \n- MTB: 105 \u00d7 500 = $52,500  \n- BMX: 45 \u00d7 250 = $11,250  \n- Trekking: 150 \u00d7 450 = $67,500  \n\nTotal = 52,500 + 11,250 + 67,500 = $131,250  \n\nAnswer: $131,250", "correct": true, "gold": "131250"}
{"qid": "gsm:20", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "MAI-Thinking-1", "resp": "First, find the cost of one candy: \r\n\r\n- Cost of 5 lollipops = 5 \u00d7 $0.40 = $2.00\r\n- Total for 5 lollipops and 4 candies = $3.20\r\n- Cost of 4 candies = $3.20 - $2.00 = $1.20\r\n- Cost of 1 candy = $1.20 \u00f7 4 = $0.30\r\n\r\nNow, calculate the cost of 10 lollipops and 10 candies: \r\n\r\n- Cost of 10 lollipops = 10 \u00d7 $0.40 = $4.00\r\n- Cost of 10 candies = 10 \u00d7 $0.30 = $3.00\r\n- Total = $4.00 + $3.00 = $7.00\r\n\r\nAnswer: $7.00", "correct": true, "gold": "7"}
{"qid": "gsm:21", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "The pricing alternates between full price and the discounted rate. A full-price glass costs $5, so a discounted glass costs \\(0.6 \\times 5 = 3\\).\nFor an even quantity of 16 glasses there are exactly 8 glasses at each rate:\n\\[\n8 \\times 5 + 8 \\times 3 = 40 + 24 = 64\n\\]\n(The same total is obtained whether the sequence begins with a full-price or a discounted glass, because the counts of each type remain identical.)\nAnswer: 64", "correct": true, "gold": "64"}
{"qid": "gsm:22", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5", "resp": "**Step 1: Find the number of each bike type sold**\n\n- Total bikes sold = 300\n- Trekking bikes = 50% \u00d7 300 = 150 bikes\n- BMX bikes = 15% \u00d7 300 = 45 bikes\n- MTB bikes = 300 - 150 - 45 = 105 bikes\n\n**Step 2: Determine the price of each bike**\n\n- MTB = $500\n- BMX = half of MTB = $500 \u00f7 2 = $250\n- Trekking = $450\n\n**Step 3: Calculate revenue from each type**\n\n- Trekking: 150 \u00d7 $450 = $67,500\n- BMX: 45 \u00d7 $250 = $11,250\n- MTB: 105 \u00d7 $500 = $52,500\n\n**Step 4: Total earnings**\n\n$67,500 + $11,250 + $52,500 = **$131,250**\n\nAnswer: $131,250", "correct": true, "gold": "131250"}
{"qid": "gsm:22", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "Trekking bikes sold: half of 300 = 150.\nBMX bikes sold: 15% of 300 = 45.\nMTB bikes sold: 300 - 150 - 45 = 105.\nBMX price = half of 500 = 250.\nRevenue:\n- Trekking: 150 * 450 = 67500\n- BMX: 45 * 250 = 11250\n- MTB: 105 * 500 = 52500\nTotal: 67500 + 11250 + 52500 = 131250.\nAnswer: 131250", "correct": true, "gold": "131250"}
{"qid": "gsm:22", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Cohere-command-a-plus-05-2026", "resp": "<|START_TEXT|>First, determine how many of each bike were sold:\n\n- Total bikes sold = 300  \n- Trekking bikes = \u00bd\u202f\u00d7\u202f300 = 150  \n- BMX bikes = 15%\u202f\u00d7\u202f300 = 45  \n- MTB bikes = 300\u202f\u2212\u202f(150\u202f+\u202f45) = 105  \n\nNext, calculate revenue for each type:\n\n- Trekking: 150\u202f\u00d7\u202f$450 = $67,500  \n- BMX: 45\u202f\u00d7\u202f$250 = $11,250  \n- MTB: 105\u202f\u00d7\u202f$500 = $52,500  \n\nAdd the revenues together:\n\n$67,500 + $11,250 + $52,500 = $131,250  \n\nAnswer: $131,250.<|END_TEXT|>", "correct": true, "gold": "131250"}
{"qid": "gsm:23", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "DeepSeek-V4-Flash", "resp": "Let\u2019s break it down step by step.\n\n- First bank: $4000  \n- Second bank: twice as much as the first, so \\( 2 \\times 4000 = 8000 \\)  \n- Total from banks: \\( 4000 + 8000 = 12000 \\)  \n- He initially had $5000 in capital.  \n- New total capital: \\( 5000 + 12000 = 17000 \\)\n\nAnswer: 17000", "correct": true, "gold": "17000"}
{"qid": "gsm:22", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "Here's the step-by-step calculation:\n\n**Prices:**\n- MTB: $500\n- BMX: $500 \u00f7 2 = $250\n- Trekking: $450\n\n**Units sold:**\n- Total bikes: 300\n- Trekking: 300 \u00d7 50% = 150 bikes\n- BMX: 300 \u00d7 15% = 45 bikes\n- MTB: 300 \u2212 150 \u2212 45 = 105 bikes\n\n**Revenue by type:**\n- Trekking: 150 \u00d7 $450 = $67,500\n- BMX: 45 \u00d7 $250 = $11,250\n- MTB: 105 \u00d7 $500 = $52,500\n\n**Total earnings:**\n$67,500 + $11,250 + $52,500 = $131,250\n\nAnswer: $131,250", "correct": true, "gold": "131250"}
