{"qid": "gsm:21", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "MAI-Thinking-1", "resp": "Kylar buys 16 glasses. Since every second glass costs only 60% of the price: \r\n\r\n- Full price per glass: $5\r\n- Discounted price (every second glass): 60% of $5 = $3\r\n\r\nFor 16 glasses, that means 8 are at full price and 8 are at the discounted price. \r\n\r\nCalculation: (8 \u00d7 $5) + (8 \u00d7 $3) = $40 + $24 = $64\r\n\r\nAnswer: $64", "correct": true, "gold": "64"}
