{"qid": "gsm:24", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Cohere-command-a-plus-05-2026", "resp": "<|START_TEXT|>Let \\(T\\) be Timothy\u2019s locker volume.  \nZack\u2019s locker is half of Timothy\u2019s: \\(Z = \\frac{T}{2}\\).  \nPeter\u2019s locker is one\u2011fourth of Zack\u2019s: \\(P = \\frac{Z}{4} = \\frac{T}{8}\\).  \n\nGiven \\(P = 5\\) cubic inches, we solve \\(\\frac{T}{8} = 5\\), so \\(T = 5 \\times 8 = 40\\).\n\nAnswer: 40<|END_TEXT|>", "correct": true, "gold": "40"}
{"qid": "gsm:24", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "Zack's locker is half Timothy's, so if Timothy's is \\(T\\), Zack's is \\(T/2\\).\nPeter's locker is one-quarter Zack's, so Peter's is \\((T/2)/4 = T/8\\).\nGiven Peter's locker is 5 cubic inches, \\(T/8 = 5\\), therefore \\(T = 40\\).\n(Alternatively: Zack's = \\(5 \\times 4 = 20\\); Timothy's = \\(20 \\times 2 = 40\\).)\nAnswer: 40", "correct": true, "gold": "40"}
