{"qid": "gsm:26", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "Let $d$ be the time Donovan's part took and $b$ be the time Betsy's part took.\n\nFrom the problem:\n- $b = d + 18$ (Betsy took 18 minutes longer)\n- $b + d = 98$ (total time was 98 minutes)\n\nSubstituting the first equation into the second:\n$$(d + 18) + d = 98$$\n$$2d + 18 = 98$$\n$$2d = 80$$\n$$d = 40$$\n\nTherefore, Betsy's part took $40 + 18 = 58$ minutes.\n\nAnswer: 58", "correct": true, "gold": "58"}
{"qid": "gsm:25", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "The problem states that 20 trucks were dispatched, each carrying 20 tons of fertilizer. This means a total of 400 tons left the store.\n\nA quarter of those 20 vehicles suffered mechanical failure and therefore delivered nothing:  \n\\( \\frac{1}{4} \\times 20 = 5 \\) trucks failed, carrying \\( 5 \\times 20 = 100 \\) tons that never reached any farmer.\n\nThe remaining 15 trucks completed their deliveries:  \n\\( 15 \\times 20 = 300 \\) tons.\n\nNo further information (distance, time, or partial off-loading) is supplied that would alter the delivered quantity, so the total that reached the farmers is 300 tons.\n\nAnswer: 300 tons", "correct": true, "gold": "300"}
