{"qid": "gsm:26", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "Let Donovan's part of the meal take \\(d\\) minutes. Then Betsy's part took \\(d + 18\\) minutes.  \n\nBecause the two parts were performed sequentially, their durations sum to the total time required to make the meal:  \n\\[\nd + (d + 18) = 98.\n\\]  \nSimplifying the left-hand side gives  \n\\[\n2d + 18 = 98.\n\\]  \nSubtracting 18 from both sides yields  \n\\[\n2d = 80,\n\\]  \nso  \n\\[\nd = 40.\n\\]  \nBetsy's part is therefore  \n\\[\n40 + 18 = 58\n\\]  \nminutes long.  \n\n(The parallel-work interpretation is ruled out because it would make the answer trivially equal to the given total time of 98 minutes, rendering the \u201c18 minutes longer\u201d information superfluous.)\n\nAnswer: 58 minutes", "correct": true, "gold": "58"}
