{"qid": "gsm:38", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5", "resp": "**Setting up equations:**\n\nLet c = camels (2 humps each), d = dromedaries (1 hump each)\n\n- Heads: c + d = 180\n- Humps: 2c + d = 304\n\n**Solving:**\n\nSubtract the first equation from the second:\n(2c + d) \u2212 (c + d) = 304 \u2212 180\nc = 124\n\nThen: d = 180 \u2212 124 = 56\n\n**Answer: 56**", "correct": true, "gold": "56"}
{"qid": "gsm:38", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "DeepSeek-V4-Flash", "resp": "Let\u2019s define:\n\n- Let \\( c \\) = number of camels (2 humps each)  \n- Let \\( d \\) = number of dromedaries (1 hump each)\n\nWe know:\n\n1. Heads: \\( c + d = 180 \\)  \n2. Humps: \\( 2c + 1d = 304 \\)\n\nSubtract the first equation from the second:\n\n\\[\n(2c + d) - (c + d) = 304 - 180\n\\]\n\\[\nc = 124\n\\]\n\nThen:\n\n\\[\nd = 180 - 124 = 56\n\\]\n\nAnswer: 56", "correct": true, "gold": "56"}
{"qid": "gsm:38", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "Let $c$ be the number of camels and $d$ be the number of dromedaries.\n\nSince each animal has one head:\n$$c + d = 180$$\n\nSince camels have 2 humps and dromedaries have 1 hump:\n$$2c + d = 304$$\n\nSubtracting the first equation from the second:\n$$(2c + d) - (c + d) = 304 - 180$$\n$$c = 124$$\n\nSubstituting back:\n$$124 + d = 180$$\n$$d = 56$$\n\nVerification: $124$ camels contribute $248$ humps and $56$ dromedaries contribute $56$ humps, totaling $304$ humps.\n\nAnswer: 56", "correct": true, "gold": "56"}
{"qid": "gsm:39", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "openai/gpt-5.4", "resp": "First bag: 300\n\nSecond bag: 300 + 12 = 312\n\nThird bag: half of 300 = 150\n\nTotal: 300 + 312 + 150 = 762\n\nAnswer: 762", "correct": true, "gold": "762"}
{"qid": "gsm:38", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "Let \\(C\\) be camels and \\(D\\) be dromedaries.\nHeads give the equation \\(C + D = 180\\).\nHumps (bumps) give the equation \\(2C + D = 304\\).\nSubtract the first equation from the second: \\(C = 124\\).\nThus \\(D = 180 - 124 = 56\\).\nVerification: total humps are \\(2 \\times 124 + 56 = 304\\).\nAnswer: 56", "correct": true, "gold": "56"}
{"qid": "gsm:38", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Cohere-command-a-plus-05-2026", "resp": "<|START_TEXT|>Let \\(c\\) be the number of camels and \\(d\\) the number of dromedaries.\n\n- Each animal has one head:\u2003\\(c + d = 180\\)\n- Camels have 2 humps, dromedaries 1 hump:\u2003\\(2c + d = 304\\)\n\nSubtract the first equation from the second:\n\\[\n(2c + d) - (c + d) = 304 - 180 \\;\\Rightarrow\\; c = 124\n\\]\n\nThen\n\\[\nd = 180 - c = 180 - 124 = 56\n\\]\n\nAnswer: 56<|END_TEXT|>", "correct": true, "gold": "56"}
