{"qid": "gsm:40", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5", "resp": "**Setting up equations:**\n- Let David = D\n- Lily = D + 7\n- Bodhi = 2D (since David found half of Bodhi's amount)\n\n**Solving:**\n(D + 7) + D + 2D = 43\n4D + 7 = 43\n4D = 36\nD = 9\n\n**Finding Lily's insects:**\nLily = D + 7 = 9 + 7 = 16\n\n**Check:** David = 9, Lily = 16, Bodhi = 18 \u2192 9 + 16 + 18 = 43 \u2713\n\nAnswer: 16", "correct": true, "gold": "16"}
{"qid": "gsm:40", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "Let $D$ be the number of insects David found.\n\nSince David found half of what Bodhi found, Bodhi found $2D$ insects.\n\nSince Lily found 7 more than David, Lily found $D + 7$ insects.\n\nTogether they found 43 insects:\n$$D + 2D + (D + 7) = 43$$\n$$4D + 7 = 43$$\n$$4D = 36$$\n$$D = 9$$\n\nTherefore, Lily found $9 + 7 = 16$ insects.\n\nAnswer: 16", "correct": true, "gold": "16"}
