{"qid": "gsm:41", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "openai/gpt-5.4", "resp": "Let Grandma\u2019s speed on the beach be \\(b\\) miles per minute.\n\nShe walks 2 miles on the beach in 40 minutes, so:\n\\[\nb = \\frac{2}{40} = \\frac{1}{20}\n\\]\nSo her beach speed is \\(\\frac{1}{20}\\) mile per minute.\n\nOn the sidewalk, she walks twice as fast:\n\\[\n2b = 2 \\cdot \\frac{1}{20} = \\frac{1}{10}\n\\]\nSo her sidewalk speed is \\(\\frac{1}{10}\\) mile per minute.\n\nShe walks 1 mile on the sidewalk, so the time for that is:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{1/10} = 10 \\text{ minutes}\n\\]\n\nTotal time:\n\\[\n40 + 10 = 50\n\\]\n\nAnswer: 50", "correct": true, "gold": "50"}
