{"qid": "gsm:41", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "Let $v_b$ be Grandma's speed on the beach and $v_s$ be her speed on the sidewalk.\n\nFrom the problem:\n- $v_s = 2v_b$\n- Beach distance = 2 miles, time on beach = 40 minutes\n- Sidewalk distance = 1 mile\n\nUsing $\\text{speed} = \\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{time}}$ for the beach:\n$$v_b = \\frac{2\\text{ miles}}{40\\text{ min}} = \\frac{1}{20}\\text{ miles per minute}$$\n\nTherefore, her speed on the sidewalk is:\n$$v_s = 2 \\times \\frac{1}{20} = \\frac{1}{10}\\text{ miles per minute}$$\n\nTime spent on the sidewalk:\n$$\\text{time} = \\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{speed}} = \\frac{1}{\\frac{1}{10}} = 10\\text{ minutes}$$\n\nTotal time for the entire walk:\n$$40\\text{ minutes} + 10\\text{ minutes} = 50\\text{ minutes}$$\n\nAnswer: 50", "correct": true, "gold": "50"}
{"qid": "gsm:40", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "MAI-Thinking-1", "resp": "Let\u2019s solve the problem step by step:\n\n- Let **D** be the number of insects David found.\n- Lily found 7 more than David, so **L = D + 7**.\n- David found half of what Bodhi found, so **D = B \u00f7 2**, which means **B = 2D**.\n- Together they collected 43: **L + D + B = 43**.\n\nSubstitute the values:\n(D + 7) + D + 2D = 43\n4D + 7 = 43\n4D = 36\nD = 9\n\nNow, find Lily\u2019s total: L = D + 7 = 9 + 7 = 16.\n\nAnswer: 16", "correct": true, "gold": "16"}
{"qid": "gsm:37", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "The problem provides the price of one CD and the combined total paid for that CD plus the headphone set. Subtracting gives the implied cost of the headphone set alone:\n\n\\[\n48 - 4 = 44\n\\]\n\nDividing the headphone-set cost by the unit price of a CD shows how many additional CDs could have been purchased with that same amount of money:\n\n\\[\n44 \\div 4 = 11\n\\]\n\nThus, forgoing the headphone set would have freed up exactly enough money for 11 more CDs.\n\nAnswer: 11", "correct": true, "gold": "11"}
