{"qid": "gsm:45", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "openai/gpt-5.4", "resp": "Anakin caught:\n- 10 starfish\n- 6 sea horses\n- 3 clownfish\n\nSo Anakin\u2019s total is 10 + 6 + 3 = 19.\n\nLocsin caught:\n- 5 fewer starfish than 10 \u2192 5\n- 3 fewer sea horses than 6 \u2192 3\n- 2 more clownfish than 3 \u2192 5\n\nSo Locsin\u2019s total is 5 + 3 + 5 = 13.\n\nTogether they caught 19 + 13 = 32.\n\nAnswer: 32", "correct": true, "gold": "32"}
{"qid": "gsm:45", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "DeepSeek-V4-Flash", "resp": "Let's break it down step by step.\n\n**Anakin's catch:**  \n- Starfish: 10  \n- Sea horses: 6  \n- Clownfish: 3  \n\n**Locsin's catch:**  \n- Starfish: 10 \u2212 5 = 5  \n- Sea horses: 6 \u2212 3 = 3  \n- Clownfish: 3 + 2 = 5  \n\n**Total fish (clownfish are fish; starfish and sea horses are not fish):**  \nAnakin's clownfish: 3  \nLocsin's clownfish: 5  \nTotal fish = 3 + 5 = 8  \n\nAnswer: 8", "correct": false, "gold": "32"}
{"qid": "gsm:45", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5", "resp": "Anakin caught: 10 + 6 + 3 = 19 fish\nLocsin caught: (10-5) + (6-3) + (3+2) = 5 + 3 + 5 = 13 fish\n\nTotal: 19 + 13 = 32\n\nAnswer: 32", "correct": true, "gold": "32"}
{"qid": "gsm:46", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "openai/gpt-5.4", "resp": "Total toys needed: 400.\n\nAfter the 10-hour shift, they are still 20 toys short, so they completed:\n\n400 - 20 = 380 toys\n\nLet the fifth worker produce \\(x\\) toys per hour.\n\nIn 1 hour, the 5 workers together produce:\n\n- 2 workers at 6 toys/hour: \\(2 \\times 6 = 12\\)\n- 2 workers at 4 toys/hour: \\(2 \\times 4 = 8\\)\n- 1 worker at \\(x\\) toys/hour: \\(x\\)\n\nSo total hourly production is:\n\n12 + 8 + x = 20 + x\n\nIn 10 hours, they produce:\n\n10(20 + x) = 380\n\nSolve:\n\n20 + x = 38  \nx = 18\n\nAnswer: 18 toys per hour", "correct": true, "gold": "18"}
{"qid": "gsm:45", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Cohere-command-a-plus-05-2026", "resp": "<|START_TEXT|>Anakin caught 10 starfish, 6 sea horses, and 3 clownfish.  \nLocsin caught 5 fewer starfish (10\u202f\u2212\u202f5\u202f=\u202f5), 3 fewer sea horses (6\u202f\u2212\u202f3\u202f=\u202f3), and 2 more clownfish (3\u202f+\u202f2\u202f=\u202f5).\n\nTotal starfish: 10\u202f+\u202f5\u202f=\u202f15  \nTotal sea horses: 6\u202f+\u202f3\u202f=\u202f9  \nTotal clownfish: 3\u202f+\u202f5\u202f=\u202f8  \n\nCombined total fish: 15\u202f+\u202f9\u202f+\u202f8\u202f=\u202f32  \n\nAnswer: 32<|END_TEXT|>", "correct": true, "gold": "32"}
{"qid": "gsm:46", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5", "resp": "**18 toys per hour**\n\nCalculation:\n- Workers 1&2: 2 \u00d7 6 toys/hr \u00d7 10 hrs = 120 toys\n- Workers 3&4: 2 \u00d7 4 toys/hr \u00d7 10 hrs = 80 toys\n- Total from these 4 workers: 200 toys\n\nTotal produced by all 5 workers = 400 \u2212 20 = 380 toys\n\nFifth worker's total production = 380 \u2212 200 = 180 toys over 10 hours\n\nRate = 180 \u00f7 10 = **18 toys per hour**\n\nAnswer: 18", "correct": true, "gold": "18"}
{"qid": "gsm:46", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "DeepSeek-V4-Flash", "resp": "Let\u2019s break it down step by step.\n\n- Total toys needed: 400  \n- After the shift, 20 toys are still needed, so toys produced during the shift = 400 \u2212 20 = 380 toys.  \n- Shift length: 10 hours.  \n\n**Workers and their rates:**  \n- 2 workers at 6 toys/hour each \u2192 together: 2 \u00d7 6 = 12 toys/hour  \n- 2 workers at 4 toys/hour each \u2192 together: 2 \u00d7 4 = 8 toys/hour  \n- So the first 4 workers produce 12 + 8 = 20 toys/hour total.  \n\nIn 10 hours, those 4 workers produce:  \n20 \u00d7 10 = 200 toys.  \n\nRemaining toys produced by the fifth worker:  \n380 \u2212 200 = 180 toys in 10 hours.  \n\nSo the fifth worker\u2019s rate:  \n180 \u00f7 10 = 18 toys per hour.\n\nAnswer: 18", "correct": true, "gold": "18"}
{"qid": "gsm:46", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "Here's the step-by-step calculation:\n\n**Total toys needed:** 400  \n**Toys still needed after shift:** 20  \n**Toys actually produced:** 400 - 20 = 380 toys\n\n**Production from first 4 workers:**\n- 2 workers \u00d7 6 toys/hour \u00d7 10 hours = 120 toys\n- 2 workers \u00d7 4 toys/hour \u00d7 10 hours = 80 toys\n- **Subtotal:** 200 toys\n\n**Production from fifth worker:**\n380 total toys - 200 toys = 180 toys\n\n**Hourly rate of fifth worker:**\n180 toys \u00f7 10 hours = 18 toys per hour\n\nAnswer: 18", "correct": true, "gold": "18"}
{"qid": "gsm:45", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "MAI-Thinking-1", "resp": "**Reasoning:** \r\n\r\n1. **Locsin's catch:** \r\n   - Starfish: 10 - 5 = 5\r\n   - Sea horses: 6 - 3 = 3\r\n   - Clownfish: 3 + 2 = 5\r\n   Total for Locsin = 5 + 3 + 5 = 13\r\n\r\n2. **Anakin's catch:** \r\n   - Starfish: 10, Sea horses: 6, Clownfish: 3\r\n   Total for Anakin = 10 + 6 + 3 = 19\r\n\r\n3. **Total fish:** 19 + 13 = 32\r\n\r\nAnswer: 32", "correct": true, "gold": "32"}
{"qid": "gsm:41", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "The trail consists of a total distance of 3 miles, specifically 2 miles on the beach followed by 1 mile on the sidewalk. The time spent on the beach portion is given as 40 minutes, which directly determines the beach walking speed:\n\\[\nv_{\\text{beach}} = \\frac{2 \\text{ miles}}{40 \\text{ minutes}} = \\frac{1}{20} \\text{ miles per minute}.\n\\]\nThe sidewalk speed is twice the beach speed:\n\\[\nv_{\\text{sidewalk}} = 2 \\times \\frac{1}{20} = \\frac{1}{10} \\text{ miles per minute}.\n\\]\nThe time required for the 1-mile sidewalk segment is therefore\n\\[\nt_{\\text{sidewalk}} = \\frac{1 \\text{ mile}}{\\frac{1}{10} \\text{ miles per minute}} = 10 \\text{ minutes}.\n\\]\nAdding the two segments yields the total time for the full 3-mile walk:\n\\[\n40 + 10 = 50 \\text{ minutes}.\n\\]\nAnswer: 50", "correct": true, "gold": "50"}
{"qid": "gsm:45", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "Anakin caught $10 + 6 + 3 = 19$ sea creatures.\n\nLocsin caught:\n- $10 - 5 = 5$ starfish\n- $6 - 3 = 3$ sea horses  \n- $3 + 2 = 5$ clownfish\nTotal for Locsin: $5 + 3 + 5 = 13$ sea creatures.\n\nTogether they caught $19 + 13 = 32$ animals in total.\n\n*(Note: While starfish are not biologically fish, and sea horses are fish, the problem likely uses \"fish\" to mean the total catch. If counting only true fish\u2014sea horses and clownfish\u2014the total would be $9 + 8 = 17$.)*\n\nAnswer: 32", "correct": true, "gold": "32"}
{"qid": "gsm:46", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Cohere-command-a-plus-05-2026", "resp": "<|START_TEXT|>The two workers producing 6 toys per hour together make \\(2 \\times 6 = 12\\) toys per hour, which over 10 hours yields \\(12 \\times 10 = 120\\) toys.  \nThe two workers producing 4 toys per hour together make \\(2 \\times 4 = 8\\) toys per hour, which over 10 hours yields \\(8 \\times 10 = 80\\) toys.  \n\nTogether these four workers produce \\(120 + 80 = 200\\) toys in the 10\u2011hour shift.  \n\nSince the order requires 400 toys and they are short by 20, they actually produced \\(400 - 20 = 380\\) toys.  \n\nLet the fifth worker\u2019s rate be \\(r\\) toys per hour. Over 10 hours he contributes \\(10r\\) toys, so:\n\n\\[\n200 + 10r = 380 \\\\\n10r = 180 \\\\\nr = 18\n\\]\n\nThus the fifth worker produces **18 toys per hour**.\n\nAnswer: 18<|END_TEXT|>", "correct": true, "gold": "18"}
