{"qid": "gsm:46", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "The order requires a total of 400 toys. After one 10-hour shift, 20 toys are still needed, which means exactly 380 toys were produced during the shift.\n\nThe four workers with known rates contribute the following:\n- 2 workers each produce 6 toys per hour, for a combined output of \\(2 \\times 6 \\times 10 = 120\\) toys.\n- 2 workers each produce 4 toys per hour, for a combined output of \\(2 \\times 4 \\times 10 = 80\\) toys.\n\nThese four workers therefore account for 200 toys in total. The remaining \\(380 - 200 = 180\\) toys must have been produced by the fifth worker. Over the 10-hour shift that corresponds to a rate of \\(180 / 10 = 18\\) toys per hour.\n\nAnswer: 18", "correct": true, "gold": "18"}
