{"qid": "gsm:52", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "The problem breaks down into three distinct phases of tooth payments, which must be calculated sequentially based on the stated rules.\n\n- Phase 1 covers the first tooth only, which yields a flat payment of 5.\n- Phase 2 covers the next three teeth, each paid at the stated rate of 1, for a subtotal of 3.\n- Phase 3 covers the final two teeth. The rule states that each of these teeth receives half the per-tooth amount given for each of the immediately preceding three teeth. That preceding per-tooth amount is 1, so half of it is 0.5; therefore the two teeth produce a subtotal of 1.\n\nSumming the three subtotals produces the overall total payment.\n\nAnswer: 9", "correct": true, "gold": "9"}
