{"qid": "gsm:55", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "openai/gpt-5.4", "resp": "George started with $5.  \nHe had 1% of his money left, so he spent 99% of $5:\n\n\\[\n0.99 \\times 5 = 4.95\n\\]\n\nSo George spent $4.95 total.\n\nHe bought 3 bags of chips at 40 cents each:\n\n\\[\n3 \\times 0.40 = 1.20\n\\]\n\nMoney spent on candy bars:\n\n\\[\n4.95 - 1.20 = 3.75\n\\]\n\nEach candy bar costs 75 cents:\n\n\\[\n3.75 \\div 0.75 = 5\n\\]\n\nAnswer: 5", "correct": true, "gold": "5"}
{"qid": "gsm:40", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "DeepSeek-V4-Flash", "resp": "Let\u2019s define:\n\n- Let \\( b \\) = number Bodhi found.  \n- David found half of Bodhi: \\( d = \\frac{b}{2} \\).  \n- Lily found 7 more than David: \\( l = \\frac{b}{2} + 7 \\).  \n\nTogether:  \n\\[\nb + \\frac{b}{2} + \\left(\\frac{b}{2} + 7\\right) = 43\n\\]  \n\\[\nb + \\frac{b}{2} + \\frac{b}{2} + 7 = 43\n\\]  \n\\[\nb + b + 7 = 43\n\\]  \n\\[\n2b + 7 = 43\n\\]  \n\\[\n2b = 36\n\\]  \n\\[\nb = 18\n\\]  \n\nThen David: \\( d = 9 \\), Lily: \\( l = 9 + 7 = 16 \\).\n\nAnswer: 16", "correct": true, "gold": "16"}
