{"qid": "gsm:54", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "MAI-Thinking-1", "resp": "Let Azibo's points be $A$. \r\n\r\nFrom the problem: \r\n\r\n- Bahati scored 20 more than Azibo: $B = A + 20$\r\n- Bahati scored 10 more than Dinar: $B = D + 10$, so $D = B - 10 = A + 10$\r\n- Total points: $A + B + D = 45$\r\n\r\nSubstitute the values: \r\n\r\n$A + (A + 20) + (A + 10) = 45$\r\n\r\n$3A + 30 = 45$\r\n\r\n$3A = 15$\r\n\r\n$A = 5$\r\n\r\nAnswer: 5", "correct": true, "gold": "5"}
