{"qid": "gsm:55", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "George started with $\\$5$. Having $1\\%$ of his money left means he spent $99\\%$ of $\\$5$, which is $\\$4.95$.\n\nHe bought $3$ bags of chips at $\\$0.40$ each:\n$$3 \\times \\$0.40 = \\$1.20$$\n\nThe remaining amount spent on candy bars is:\n$$\\$4.95 - \\$1.20 = \\$3.75$$\n\nEach candy bar costs $\\$0.75$, so the number of candy bars is:\n$$\\$3.75 \\div \\$0.75 = 5$$\n\nAnswer: 5", "correct": true, "gold": "5"}
{"qid": "gsm:54", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "Let \\(B\\), \\(A\\), and \\(D\\) be the points scored by Bahati, Azibo, and Dinar.\nThe conditions give the system\n\\[\nB + A + D = 45,\n\\]\n\\[\nB = A + 20,\n\\]\n\\[\nB = D + 10.\n\\]\nSubstitute the last two equations into the first:\n\\[\nB + (B-20) + (B-10) = 45 \\implies 3B - 30 = 45 \\implies 3B = 75 \\implies B = 25.\n\\]\nThus\n\\[\nA = 5, \\quad D = 15.\n\\]\nVerification: \\(25 + 5 + 15 = 45\\), Bahati\u2019s total is strictly largest, and the stated margins hold.\nAnswer: 5", "correct": true, "gold": "5"}
{"qid": "gsm:57", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "Chenny is 10 years old.  \nAlyana is 4 years younger than Chenny, so Alyana is $10 - 4 = 6$ years old.  \nAnne is 2 years older than Alyana, so Anne is $6 + 2 = 8$ years old.\n\nAnswer: 8", "correct": true, "gold": "8"}
