{"qid": "gsm:55", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "MAI-Thinking-1", "resp": "He had $5.00 total and 1% left, so he spent 99% of $5.00: $5.00 \u00d7 0.99 = $4.95. \r\n\r\nHe bought 3 bags of chips at 40 cents each: 3 \u00d7 $0.40 = $1.20. \r\n\r\nThe amount spent on candy bars is $4.95 - $1.20 = $3.75. \r\n\r\nEach candy bar costs 75 cents, so the number bought is $3.75 \u00f7 $0.75 = 5. \r\n\r\nAnswer: 5", "correct": true, "gold": "5"}
