{"qid": "gsm:56", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Cohere-command-a-plus-05-2026", "resp": "<|START_TEXT|>Martha started collecting shells at age 5 and collects one each month. From age 5 to age 10 is a span of 5 years. \n\n\\(5 \\text{ years} \\times 12 \\text{ months/year} = 60 \\text{ months}\\).\n\nTherefore, by her 10th birthday she will have collected 60 shells.\n\nAnswer: 60<|END_TEXT|>", "correct": true, "gold": "60"}
{"qid": "gsm:58", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "openai/gpt-5.4", "resp": "Let the second mug be \\(x\\) degrees.\n\nHe mixes:\n- 4 ounces at \\(33^\\circ\\)\n- 1 ounce at \\(x^\\circ\\)\n\nThe mixed temperature is the weighted average:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{4(33) + 1(x)}{5}\n\\]\n\nHe can drink it only if it's at least \\(40^\\circ\\), so:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{132 + x}{5} \\ge 40\n\\]\n\n\\[\n132 + x \\ge 200\n\\]\n\n\\[\nx \\ge 68\n\\]\n\nSo the second mug must be at least **68 degrees**.\n\nAnswer: 68 degrees", "correct": true, "gold": "68"}
{"qid": "gsm:57", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "MAI-Thinking-1", "resp": "Answer: Anne is 8 years old.", "correct": true, "gold": "8"}
{"qid": "gsm:58", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "DeepSeek-V4-Flash", "resp": "We know Donny can drink water only if it's at least 40 degrees.  \nHe pours 4 ounces from the 33-degree mug and 1 ounce from the unknown temperature mug into his water bottle.  \nThe mixture must be at least 40 degrees.\n\nLet the unknown temperature be \\( T \\).  \nThe final temperature is a weighted average:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{4 \\cdot 33 + 1 \\cdot T}{5} \\geq 40\n\\]\n\nMultiply both sides by 5:\n\n\\[\n132 + T \\geq 200\n\\]\n\n\\[\nT \\geq 68\n\\]\n\nSo the second bottle must be at least 68 degrees.\n\nAnswer: 68", "correct": true, "gold": "68"}
{"qid": "gsm:58", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "To find the minimum temperature of the second bottle, I need to calculate the weighted average temperature of the mixture.\n\nLet $x$ be the temperature of the second bottle.\n\nWhen mixing 4 ounces at 33\u00b0 and 1 ounce at $x$\u00b0, the resulting temperature is:\n$$\\frac{4(33) + 1(x)}{4 + 1} = \\frac{132 + x}{5}$$\n\nFor Donny to drink it, this must be at least 40\u00b0:\n$$\\frac{132 + x}{5} \\geq 40$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by 5:\n$$132 + x \\geq 200$$\n\nSubtracting 132 from both sides:\n$$x \\geq 68$$\n\nVerification: If the second bottle is exactly 68\u00b0, the mixture temperature is $\\frac{132 + 68}{5} = \\frac{200}{5} = 40$\u00b0, which is exactly the minimum drinkable temperature.\n\nAnswer: 68", "correct": true, "gold": "68"}
{"qid": "gsm:58", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5", "resp": "**Answer: 68 degrees**\n\nTo find the minimum temperature of the second mug, we use the weighted average formula since we're mixing 4 ounces at 33\u00b0 with 1 ounce at an unknown temperature (x), and the result must be at least 40\u00b0.\n\nSetting up the equation:\n$$\\frac{4(33) + 1(x)}{5} \\geq 40$$\n\nSolving:\n$$132 + x \\geq 200$$\n$$x \\geq 68$$\n\nAnswer: 68 degrees", "correct": true, "gold": "68"}
{"qid": "gsm:56", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "From her 5th birthday to her 10th birthday is exactly 5 years.  \nAt a rate of 1 shell per month, that interval contains 5 \u00d7 12 = 60 months, so she collects 60 shells.\n\nAnswer: 60", "correct": true, "gold": "60"}
