{"qid": "gsm:58", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "The water bottle starts empty. The mixture consists of 4 oz at 33\u00b0 and 1 oz at unknown temperature \\(T\\). For the mixture to reach a drinkable temperature, its weighted average must satisfy\n\\[\n\\frac{4 \\times 33 + 1 \\times T}{5} \\ge 40.\n\\]\nClearing the inequality yields\n\\[\n132 + T \\ge 200 \\implies T \\ge 68.\n\\]\nThus the second mug must be at least 68\u00b0 (attained when the mixture is exactly 40\u00b0).\n\nAnswer: 68 degrees", "correct": true, "gold": "68"}
