{"qid": "gsm:58", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Cohere-command-a-plus-05-2026", "resp": "<|START_TEXT|>To determine the minimum temperature \\(T\\) of the second bottle, consider the mixture\u2019s temperature after adding the two portions.\n\nThe mixture temperature is the weighted average of the two temperatures, based on their volumes:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Mixture temperature} = \\frac{4 \\times 33 + 1 \\times T}{4 + 1}\n\\]\n\nDonny can drink the water when this mixture reaches at least \\(40^\\circ\\). Set the expression greater than or equal to \\(40\\) and solve for \\(T\\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{132 + T}{5} \\ge 40 \\\\\n132 + T \\ge 200 \\\\\nT \\ge 68\n\\]\n\nThus, the second bottle must be at least \\(68^\\circ\\).\n\n**Answer:** 68 degrees.<|END_TEXT|>", "correct": true, "gold": "68"}
