{"qid": "gsm:61", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "First half:\n- Team A scores 4 goals.\n- Team B scores 2 fewer than A: $4 - 2 = 2$ goals.\n\nSecond half:\n- Team B scores 4 times its first-half total: $4 \\times 2 = 8$ goals.\n- Team A scores $\\frac{1}{4}$ of B's second-half total: $\\frac{1}{4} \\times 8 = 2$ goals.\n\nTotals:\n- Team A: $4 + 2 = 6$ goals\n- Team B: $2 + 8 = 10$ goals\n- Combined: $6 + 10 = 16$ goals\n\nAnswer: 16", "correct": true, "gold": "16"}
{"qid": "gsm:59", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "MAI-Thinking-1", "resp": "**Reasoning:** \r\n\r\n1. **Day temperature:** 45 degrees.\r\n2. **Night temperature:** 45 - 33 = 12 degrees (33 degrees colder than during the day).\r\n3. **Required temperature:** At least 32 degrees to prevent pipes from freezing.\r\n4. **Temperature increase needed:** 32 - 12 = 20 degrees.\r\n5. **Logs required:** Each log heats by 5 degrees, so 20 \u00f7 5 = 4 logs.\r\n\r\nAnswer: 4 logs", "correct": true, "gold": "4"}
{"qid": "gsm:61", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "DeepSeek-V4-Flash", "resp": "Let's break it down step by step.\n\n**First half:**  \nTeam A scores 4 goals.  \nTeam B scores 2 fewer than team A:  \n\\( 4 - 2 = 2 \\) goals.\n\n**Second half:**  \nTeam B scores 4 times what it scored in the first half:  \n\\( 2 \\times 4 = 8 \\) goals.  \nTeam A scores \\( \\frac{1}{4} \\) of what team B scores in the second half:  \n\\( \\frac{1}{4} \\times 8 = 2 \\) goals.\n\n**Total goals:**  \nFirst half: \\( 4 + 2 = 6 \\)  \nSecond half: \\( 2 + 8 = 10 \\)  \nTotal: \\( 6 + 10 = 16 \\)\n\nAnswer: 16", "correct": true, "gold": "16"}
{"qid": "gsm:61", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5", "resp": "**First half:**\n- Team A: 4 goals\n- Team B: 4 \u2212 2 = 2 goals\n\n**Second half:**\n- Team B: 4 \u00d7 2 = 8 goals\n- Team A: 8 \u00f7 4 = 2 goals\n\n**Total goals:** 4 + 2 + 2 + 8 = 16\n\nAnswer: 16", "correct": true, "gold": "16"}
{"qid": "gsm:61", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "First half:\n- Team A scores 4 goals.\n- Team B scores 2 fewer than A, so 4 - 2 = 2 goals.\nSecond half:\n- Team B scores 4 times its first-half total, so 4 * 2 = 8 goals.\n- Team A scores 1/4 of Team B's second-half total, so 1/4 * 8 = 2 goals.\nMatch totals: A has 4 + 2 = 6 goals; B has 2 + 8 = 10 goals. Grand total is therefore 6 + 10 = 16.\nAnswer: 16", "correct": true, "gold": "16"}
{"qid": "gsm:61", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Cohere-command-a-plus-05-2026", "resp": "<|START_TEXT|>First half:  \n- Team A scores 4 goals.  \n- Team B scores 2 fewer than Team A \u2192 \\(4 - 2 = 2\\) goals.\n\nSecond half:  \n- Team B scores 4 times its first\u2011half goals \u2192 \\(4 \\times 2 = 8\\) goals.  \n- Team A scores \\(\\frac{1}{4}\\) of Team B\u2019s second\u2011half goals \u2192 \\(\\frac{1}{4} \\times 8 = 2\\) goals.\n\nTotal goals:  \n\\(4 + 2 + 2 + 8 = 16\\).\n\nAnswer: 16<|END_TEXT|>", "correct": true, "gold": "16"}
{"qid": "gsm:62", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "openai/gpt-5.4", "resp": "Jack plays 20 minutes per quarter.\n\nHis 3 friends:\n- 2 worse friends: half as long as Jack, so 10 minutes per quarter each\n- 1 better friend: 1.5 times as long as Jack, so 30 minutes per quarter\n\nThey all play for 4 hours = 240 minutes.\n\nQuarters used:\n- Jack: 240 \u00f7 20 = 12\n- Worse friend 1: 240 \u00f7 10 = 24\n- Worse friend 2: 240 \u00f7 10 = 24\n- Better friend: 240 \u00f7 30 = 8\n\nTotal quarters = 12 + 24 + 24 + 8 = 68 quarters\n\nSince each quarter is $0.25:\n68 \u00d7 0.25 = $17\n\nAnswer: $17", "correct": false, "gold": "11"}
{"qid": "gsm:62", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "DeepSeek-V4-Flash", "resp": "Let's break it down.\n\n- Jack: 1 quarter \u2192 20 minutes  \n- Two friends (worse): half as long \u2192 10 minutes per quarter  \n- One friend (better): 1.5 times as long \u2192 30 minutes per quarter  \n\nThey play for 4 hours = 240 minutes.\n\nLet\u2019s find how many quarters each uses in 240 minutes:\n\n- Jack: 240 \u00f7 20 = 12 quarters  \n- Each worse friend: 240 \u00f7 10 = 24 quarters each \u2192 2 \u00d7 24 = 48 quarters  \n- Better friend: 240 \u00f7 30 = 8 quarters  \n\nTotal quarters = 12 + 48 + 8 = 68 quarters.\n\nEach quarter is $0.25, so total money = 68 \u00d7 0.25 = $17.\n\nAnswer: $17", "correct": false, "gold": "11"}
{"qid": "gsm:62", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5", "resp": "**Setting up the play time per quarter for each person:**\n\n- **Jack:** 20 minutes per quarter\n- **Two weaker friends:** half as long = 10 minutes per quarter each\n- **One stronger friend:** 1.5\u00d7 as long = 30 minutes per quarter\n\n**Total play time:** 4 hours = 240 minutes\n\n**Calculating quarters needed for each person:**\n\n- **Jack:** 240 \u00f7 20 = 12 quarters\n- **Weaker friend #1:** 240 \u00f7 10 = 24 quarters\n- **Weaker friend #2:** 240 \u00f7 10 = 24 quarters\n- **Stronger friend:** 240 \u00f7 30 = 8 quarters\n\n**Total quarters:** 12 + 24 + 24 + 8 = 68 quarters\n\n**Total money used:** 68 \u00d7 $0.25 = $17.00\n\nAnswer: $17.00", "correct": false, "gold": "11"}
{"qid": "gsm:63", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "openai/gpt-5.4", "resp": "Becky: \\(20 \\times \\$0.45 = \\$9.00\\), then minus \\$1 discount = \\$8.00.\n\nKelly: \\(20 \\times \\$0.50 = \\$10.00\\), then 10% off means \\(\\$10.00 \\times 0.10 = \\$1.00\\) discount, so she paid \\$9.00.\n\nDifference: \\(\\$9.00 - \\$8.00 = \\$1.00\\).\n\nAnswer: $1.00", "correct": true, "gold": "1"}
