{"qid": "gsm:62", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "First, convert 4 hours to minutes: $4 \\times 60 = 240$ minutes.\n\nDetermine how many minutes each person gets per quarter:\n- **Jack**: 20 minutes per quarter\n- **Two worse friends**: Half of Jack's time = $20 \\div 2 = 10$ minutes per quarter\n- **One better friend**: 1.5 times Jack's time = $20 \\times 1.5 = 30$ minutes per quarter\n\nCalculate quarters needed for each person to play 240 minutes:\n- Jack: $240 \\div 20 = 12$ quarters\n- Each worse friend: $240 \\div 10 = 24$ quarters \u2192 $24 \\times 2 = 48$ quarters total\n- Better friend: $240 \\div 30 = 8$ quarters\n\nTotal quarters: $12 + 48 + 8 = 68$ quarters\n\nConvert to dollars: $68 \\times \\$0.25 = \\$17.00$\n\nAnswer: $17.00 (or 68 quarters)", "correct": false, "gold": "11"}
