{"qid": "gsm:77", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "MAI-Thinking-1", "resp": "**Calculation:** \r\n\r\n1. **Value of twenties:** 10 \u00d7 $20 = $200\r\n2. **Value of quarters:** 140 \u00d7 $0.25 = $35\r\n3. **Spent from twenties:** (3/5) \u00d7 $200 = $120\r\n4. **Spent from quarters:** $35 (all spent)\r\n5. **Total spent:** $120 + $35 = $155\r\n\r\nAnswer: $155", "correct": true, "gold": "155"}
{"qid": "gsm:79", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "openai/gpt-5.4", "resp": "Billy helps 2 people per hour for 3 hours per day:\n\n2 \u00d7 3 = 6 people per day\n\nCount the days from March 1 to April 19, inclusive:\n- March: 31 days\n- April 1\u201319: 19 days\n\nTotal days: 31 + 19 = 50 days\n\nHe takes 20% of those days off:\n20% of 50 = 10 days off\n\nSo he works:\n50 - 10 = 40 days\n\nPeople helped:\n40 \u00d7 6 = 240\n\nAnswer: 240", "correct": true, "gold": "240"}
{"qid": "gsm:77", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "The problem involves US currency, where \"twenties\" refers to $20 bills and \"quarters\" refers to 25-cent coins.\n\nValue of the 10 twenties: \\(10 \\times 20 = 200\\) dollars.  \nShe spent \\(\\frac{3}{5}\\) of them, or 6 twenties: \\(6 \\times 20 = 120\\) dollars.\n\nValue of the 140 quarters: \\(140 \\times 0.25 = 35\\) dollars.  \nShe spent all of them, for 35 dollars.\n\nTotal spent on lunch: \\(120 + 35 = 155\\) dollars.\n\nAnswer: 155 dollars", "correct": true, "gold": "155"}
{"qid": "gsm:78", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Cohere-command-a-plus-05-2026", "resp": "<|START_TEXT|>First, determine the total number of groups:\n- 90 people \u00f7 9 people per group = 10 groups.\n\nNext, find how many of these groups had members bring seashells:\n- \\( \\frac{3}{5} \\) of 10 groups = \\( \\frac{3}{5} \\times 10 = 6 \\) groups.\n\nEach of those 6 groups has 9 members, and each member brings 2 seashells:\n- Seashells per group = 9 members \u00d7 2 seashells = 18 seashells.\n- Total seashells = 6 groups \u00d7 18 seashells per group = 108 seashells.\n\nAnswer: 108 seashells.<|END_TEXT|>", "correct": true, "gold": "108"}
{"qid": "gsm:79", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5", "resp": "**Calculating the total days:**\n- March: 31 days\n- April 1st to April 19th: 19 days\n- Total: 31 + 19 = 50 days\n\n**Days off vs. days worked:**\n- 20% of 50 days = 10 days off\n- Days worked = 50 - 10 = 40 days\n\n**People helped per day:**\n- 2 people/hour \u00d7 3 hours/day = 6 people/day\n\n**Total people helped:**\n- 40 days \u00d7 6 people/day = 240 people\n\nAnswer: 240", "correct": true, "gold": "240"}
{"qid": "gsm:79", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "First, calculate the total number of days from March 1st to April 19th:\n- March has 31 days, so March 1st to March 31st = 31 days\n- April 1st to April 19th = 19 days\n- Total = 31 + 19 = 50 days\n\nNext, calculate working days:\n- Days off = 20% of 50 = 0.20 \u00d7 50 = 10 days\n- Working days = 50 - 10 = 40 days\n\nCalculate people helped per day:\n- 2 people/hour \u00d7 3 hours/day = 6 people per day\n\nCalculate total people helped:\n- 40 days \u00d7 6 people/day = 240 people\n\nAnswer: 240", "correct": true, "gold": "240"}
{"qid": "gsm:78", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "First, find the total number of groups: $90 \\div 9 = 10$ groups.\n\nNext, find how many groups brought seashells: $\\frac{3}{5} \\times 10 = 6$ groups.\n\nEach of these 6 groups has 9 members, and each member brought 2 seashells, so each group brought $9 \\times 2 = 18$ seashells.\n\nTotal seashells: $6 \\times 18 = 108$.\n\nAnswer: 108", "correct": true, "gold": "108"}
{"qid": "gsm:79", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Cohere-command-a-plus-05-2026", "resp": "<|START_TEXT|>Billy can help 2 people per hour for 3 hours each day, so he helps \\(2 \\times 3 = 6\\) people per day.\n\nThe period from March\u202f1 to April\u202f19 includes:\n- March: 31 days\n- April\u202f1\u201119: 19 days  \nTotal days = \\(31 + 19 = 50\\).\n\nHe takes 20% of these days off: \\(0.20 \\times 50 = 10\\) days off.\n\nWorking days = \\(50 - 10 = 40\\) days.\n\nTotal people helped = \\(40 \\text{ days} \\times 6 \\text{ people/day} = 240\\) people.\n\nAnswer: 240<|END_TEXT|>", "correct": true, "gold": "240"}
{"qid": "gsm:79", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "Total days from March 1 to April 19 inclusive: 31 (March) + 19 (April) = 50.  \nHelping days after 20% off: 0.8 * 50 = 40.  \nPeople helped per day: 2 * 3 = 6.  \nTotal: 40 * 6 = 240.  \n\nAnswer: 240", "correct": true, "gold": "240"}
{"qid": "gsm:80", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "openai/gpt-5.4", "resp": "Each intersection has:\n\n- 6 poles\n- 4 street lights per pole\n\nSo, street lights per intersection:\n\n6 \u00d7 4 = 24\n\nThere are 4 intersections, so total street lights:\n\n24 \u00d7 4 = 96\n\nIf 20 are not working, then functioning street lights:\n\n96 - 20 = 76\n\nAnswer: 76", "correct": true, "gold": "76"}
