{"qid": "gsm:78", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "MAI-Thinking-1", "resp": "First, find the number of groups: 90 people \u00f7 9 people per group = 10 groups. \r\n\r\nNext, find 3/5 of those groups: (3/5) \u00d7 10 = 6 groups. \r\n\r\nSince each member in those groups brought back 2 seashells, there are 6 \u00d7 9 = 54 members total. Multiply that by 2: 54 \u00d7 2 = 108 seashells. \r\n\r\nAnswer: 108", "correct": true, "gold": "108"}
{"qid": "gsm:81", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "openai/gpt-5.4", "resp": "Blue blocks = 4.\n\nYellow blocks are twice as many as blue:\n\\(2 \\times 4 = 8\\).\n\nSo blue + yellow = \\(4 + 8 = 12\\).\n\nTotal blocks = 32, so red blocks = \\(32 - 12 = 20\\).\n\nAnswer: 20", "correct": true, "gold": "20"}
{"qid": "gsm:80", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Cohere-command-a-plus-05-2026", "resp": "<|START_TEXT|>First, find the total number of poles:  \n- 6 poles per intersection \u00d7 4 intersections = 24 poles.  \n\nNext, calculate the total number of street lights (each pole has 4 lights):  \n- 24 poles \u00d7 4 lights per pole = 96 street lights.  \n\nSubtract the non\u2011functioning lights:  \n- 96 total lights \u2013 20 non\u2011working lights = 76 functioning lights.  \n\nAnswer: 76<|END_TEXT|>", "correct": true, "gold": "76"}
{"qid": "gsm:81", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "DeepSeek-V4-Flash", "resp": "Let's break it down step by step.\n\n- Blue blocks: 4  \n- Yellow blocks: twice as many as blue \u2192 \\( 2 \\times 4 = 8 \\)  \n- Red blocks: unknown, call it \\( r \\)\n\nTotal blocks:  \n\\[\n4 + 8 + r = 32\n\\]  \n\\[\n12 + r = 32\n\\]  \n\\[\nr = 32 - 12 = 20\n\\]\n\nAnswer: 20", "correct": true, "gold": "20"}
