{"qid": "gsm:79", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "MAI-Thinking-1", "resp": "**Reasoning:** \r\n\r\n1. **Total days:** From March 1st to April 19th, there are 31 days in March plus 19 days in April, totaling **50 days**. \r\n\r\n2. **Days off:** Billy takes 20% of these days off. 20% of 50 = **10 days off**. \r\n\r\n3. **Days worked:** 50 - 10 = **40 days worked**. \r\n\r\n4. **People per day:** He helps 2 people per hour for 3 hours, so 2 \u00d7 3 = **6 people per day**. \r\n\r\n5. **Total people:** 40 days \u00d7 6 people = **240 people**. \r\n\r\nAnswer: 240", "correct": true, "gold": "240"}
{"qid": "gsm:82", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "openai/gpt-5.4", "resp": "The oven runs hotter than the setting by a constant percentage.\n\nIf setting 450 gives an actual temperature of 468, then:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{468}{450} = 1.04\n\\]\n\nSo the actual temperature is 104% of the set temperature.\n\nLet \\(x\\) be the temperature Maggie should set the oven to for an actual temperature of 520:\n\n\\[\n1.04x = 520\n\\]\n\n\\[\nx = \\frac{520}{1.04} = 500\n\\]\n\nAnswer: 500 degrees", "correct": true, "gold": "500"}
