{"qid": "gsm:82", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "DeepSeek-V4-Flash", "resp": "We know the oven runs hot by a certain percentage.  \nWhen set to 450, actual is 468.  \nThe increase is 468 - 450 = 18 degrees.  \nPercentage increase = (18 / 450) \u00d7 100% = 4%.  \n\nSo the actual temperature is 104% of the set temperature.  \nIf the recipe needs 520 degrees actual, we need to find the set temperature S such that:  \nS \u00d7 1.04 = 520  \nS = 520 / 1.04 = 500  \n\nAnswer: 500", "correct": true, "gold": "500"}
