{"qid": "gsm:82", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "The oven runs hot. When set to 450\u00b0, it reaches 468\u00b0, which is a ratio of $\\frac{468}{450} = 1.04$ (or 4% higher).\n\nTo get an actual temperature of 520\u00b0, she needs to solve:\n$$\\text{Set Temperature} \\times 1.04 = 520$$\n$$\\text{Set Temperature} = \\frac{520}{1.04} = 500$$\n\nAnswer: 500", "correct": true, "gold": "500"}
{"qid": "gsm:82", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "The oven runs hot by a fixed percentage. When set to 450 it actually produces 468, which is a ratio of exactly 468/450 = 1.04 (i.e., 4 % high). To obtain a true temperature of 520, the set point \\(S\\) must therefore satisfy\n\\[\nS \\times 1.04 = 520 \\implies S = 520 / 1.04 = 500.\n\\]\n(The same result follows from the proportion \\(S = 520 \\times 450 / 468\\), which simplifies directly to 500.)\nAnswer: 500", "correct": true, "gold": "500"}
{"qid": "gsm:83", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "DeepSeek-V4-Flash", "resp": "Let's break it down step by step.\n\nFirst, find how many packages he completes per hour:  \n50 - 10 = 40 packages per hour.\n\nNext, find how many packages he completes in an 8-hour day:  \n40 \u00d7 8 = 320 packages.\n\nThen, multiply by his pay per package:  \n320 \u00d7 $0.20 = $64.\n\nAnswer: $64", "correct": true, "gold": "64"}
