{"qid": "gsm:86", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Cohere-command-a-plus-05-2026", "resp": "<|START_TEXT|>Sarah sells her 20\u2011meter rope at \\$2 per meter, earning  \n\n\\[\n20 \\times \\$2 = \\$40.\n\\]\n\nThe new rope costs \\$1.5 per meter. With \\$40 she can purchase  \n\n\\[\n\\left\\lfloor\\frac{40}{1.5}\\right\\rfloor = 26 \\text{ meters}\n\\]\n\nof rope (since rope is typically sold in whole meters). The cost of 26 meters is  \n\n\\[\n26 \\times \\$1.5 = \\$39.\n\\]\n\nSubtracting this from her earnings leaves  \n\n\\[\n\\$40 - \\$39 = \\$1.\n\\]\n\nAnswer: \\$1.<|END_TEXT|>", "correct": false, "gold": "10"}
