{"qid": "gsm:91", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5", "resp": "**Setting up the problem:**\n\nLillian has 6 feeders total (3 homemade + 3 store-bought), and on average each attracts 20 birds, so total birds = 6 \u00d7 20 = 120.\n\nLet the store-bought feeders attract **x** birds each. Since the homemade feeders attract 10 more birds each, they attract **x + 10** birds each.\n\n**Equation:**\n\n3x + 3(x + 10) = 120\n\n3x + 3x + 30 = 120\n\n6x = 90\n\nx = 15\n\n**So:**\n- Store-bought feeders attract 15 birds each \u2192 3 \u00d7 15 = 45 birds\n- Homemade feeders attract 15 + 10 = 25 birds each \u2192 3 \u00d7 25 = 75 birds\n\n**Total birds per day:**\n\n45 + 75 = **120 birds**\n\nAnswer: 120", "correct": false, "gold": "150"}
{"qid": "gsm:92", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "James reads at a rate of 3 pages every 10 minutes.  \nTo read 18 pages, he needs \\( \\frac{18}{3} = 6 \\) sets of 3 pages.  \nEach set takes 10 minutes, so the total time is \\( 6 \\times 10 = 60 \\) minutes.\n\nAnswer: 60", "correct": true, "gold": "60"}
