{"qid": "gsm:91", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Cohere-command-a-plus-05-2026", "resp": "<|START_TEXT|>Lillian has 3 homemade feeders and 3 store\u2011bought feeders.  \nLet the store\u2011bought feeders attract \\(x\\) birds each. Then each homemade feeder attracts \\(x+10\\) birds.\n\nThe initial observation that \u201ceach bird feeder seems to attract 20 birds\u201d can be interpreted as the average number of birds per feeder being 20.  \n\nAverage per feeder:\n\\[\n\\frac{3x + 3(x+10)}{6} = \\frac{6x + 30}{6} = x + 5.\n\\]\n\nSet this equal to 20:\n\\[\nx + 5 = 20 \\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x = 15.\n\\]\n\nThus:\n- Store\u2011bought feeders: \\(15\\) birds each \u2192 \\(3 \\times 15 = 45\\) birds.\n- Homemade feeders: \\(15 + 10 = 25\\) birds each \u2192 \\(3 \\times 25 = 75\\) birds.\n\nTotal birds per day:\n\\[\n45 + 75 = 120.\n\\]\n\nAnswer: 120 birds.<|END_TEXT|>", "correct": false, "gold": "150"}
