{"qid": "gsm:92", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "MAI-Thinking-1", "resp": "**Reasoning:** \r\n\r\nJames reads at a rate of 10 minutes for 3 pages. To find how long it takes him to read 18 pages, we can set up a proportion: \r\n\r\n$\\frac{10 \\text{ minutes}}{3 \\text{ pages}} = \\frac{x \\text{ minutes}}{18 \\text{ pages}}$ \r\n\r\nSolving for $x$: \r\n\r\n$x = \\frac{10 \\times 18}{3} = \\frac{180}{3} = 60$ minutes. \r\n\r\nAnswer: 60 minutes", "correct": true, "gold": "60"}
