{"qid": "gsm:102", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "The total period of visits is 8 years (5 years before the price increase + 3 years after).  \nThis produces 8 years \u00d7 3 visits/year = 24 visits in total.  \n\nFor the first 5 years the price remains $2 per visit, giving 5 \u00d7 3 = 15 visits at the original price:  \n15 \u00d7 $2 = $30.  \n\nAfter year 5 the price rises by 150 %, so the new price is $2 + (1.5 \u00d7 $2) = $5.  \nThe remaining 3 years therefore produce 3 \u00d7 3 = 9 visits at the new price:  \n9 \u00d7 $5 = $45.  \n\nAdding the two periods yields the overall expenditure:  \n$30 + $45 = $75.  \n\nAnswer: $75", "correct": true, "gold": "75"}
