{"qid": "gsm:107", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "There are 8 babies total.\n\n- Purple wearers: $\\frac{3}{4} \\times 8 = 6$ babies\n- Blue wearers: $\\frac{1}{4} \\times 8 = 2$ babies\n\nBows:\n- All 2 blue-wearers wear bows\n- $\\frac{1}{3}$ of the 6 purple-wearers wear bows = 2 babies\n\nTotal babies wearing bows: $2 + 2 = 4$\nPurple-wearers wearing bows: 2\n\nThe probability is $\\frac{2}{4} = \\frac{1}{2} = 50\\%$.\n\nAnswer: 50%", "correct": true, "gold": "50"}
{"qid": "gsm:107", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Cohere-command-a-plus-05-2026", "resp": "<|START_TEXT|>First, determine how many babies wear each color:\n- Total babies = 8\n- Purple wearers = \\( \\frac{3}{4} \\times 8 = 6 \\)\n- Blue wearers = \\( \\frac{1}{4} \\times 8 = 2 \\)\n\nNext, find how many of each group wear bows:\n- All blue wearers wear bows \u2192 2 babies\n- \\( \\frac{1}{3} \\) of purple wearers wear bows \u2192 \\( \\frac{1}{3} \\times 6 = 2 \\) babies\n\nTotal babies wearing bows = \\(2 + 2 = 4\\).\n\nOf these bow-wearers, the ones in purple are the 2 purple-wearers with bows.\n\nThe probability that a randomly chosen bow-wearer is wearing purple is:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\text{purple bow-wearers}}{\\text{total bow-wearers}} = \\frac{2}{4} = \\frac{1}{2} = 0.5\n\\]\n\nConvert to a percentage: \\(0.5 \\times 100\\% = 50\\%\\).\n\nAnswer: 50%<|END_TEXT|>", "correct": true, "gold": "50"}
{"qid": "gsm:108", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "openai/gpt-5.4", "resp": "Ava gets compared to Emma:\n\n- Enemies: 8 more \u00d7 10 points = +80\n- Berries: 3 more \u00d7 5 points = +15\n- Time: 4 seconds slower = 4 fewer seconds left, so 4 \u00d7 30 = -120\n\nTotal difference:\n80 + 15 - 120 = -25\n\nSo Ava scores 25 fewer points than Emma.\n\nAnswer: 25 points, with Emma scoring higher.", "correct": true, "gold": "25"}
{"qid": "gsm:107", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5", "resp": "**Setup:**\n- Total octuplets = 8\n- Purple: 3/4 \u00d7 8 = 6 babies\n- Blue: 1/4 \u00d7 8 = 2 babies\n\n**Bow wearers:**\n- All blue-wearers wear bows: 2 babies\n- 1/3 of purple-wearers wear bows: 1/3 \u00d7 6 = 2 babies\n- Total bow wearers: 2 + 2 = 4 babies\n\n**Chance a bow-wearer is wearing purple:**\n- Purple bow-wearers = 2\n- Total bow-wearers = 4\n- Percentage = 2/4 = 50%\n\nAnswer: 50%", "correct": true, "gold": "50"}
{"qid": "gsm:107", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "There are 8 babies total. This means 6 wear purple and 2 wear blue.\nAll 2 blue babies wear bows, and \\( \\frac13 \\) of the purple babies (i.e., 2) also wear bows.\nThus 4 babies total wear bows, of which exactly 2 wear purple.\nThe desired conditional probability is therefore exactly \\( \\frac24 = 50\\% \\).\nEquivalently, via the definition of conditional probability:\n\\[\nP(\\text{purple} \\mid \\text{bow}) = \\frac{P(\\text{purple and bow})}{P(\\text{bow})} = \\frac{\\frac34 \\cdot \\frac13}{\\frac34 \\cdot \\frac13 + \\frac14 \\cdot 1} = \\frac{\\frac14}{\\frac12} = 50\\%.\n\\]\nAnswer: 50%", "correct": true, "gold": "50"}
