{"qid": "gsm:96", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "DeepSeek-V4-Flash", "resp": "Let\u2019s break it down step by step.\n\n1. Blue ties cost $40 each, and he spent $200 on blue ties.  \n   Number of blue ties = \\( \\frac{200}{40} = 5 \\).\n\n2. He buys twice as many red ties as blue ties.  \n   Number of red ties = \\( 2 \\times 5 = 10 \\).\n\n3. Red ties cost 50% more than blue ties.  \n   Cost of a red tie = \\( 40 \\times 1.5 = 60 \\) dollars.\n\n4. Cost of red ties = \\( 10 \\times 60 = 600 \\) dollars.\n\n5. Total spent = blue ties ($200) + red ties ($600) = $800.\n\nAnswer: 800", "correct": true, "gold": "800"}
