{"qid": "gsm:108", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "Let \\(E\\), \\(B\\), and \\(T\\) denote Emma's enemies jumped, berries collected, and seconds remaining, respectively.\nAva's corresponding values are then \\(E + 8\\), \\(B + 3\\), and \\(T - 4\\).\nEmma's score is \\(10E + 5B + 30T\\).\nAva's score expands to\n\\[\n10(E + 8) + 5(B + 3) + 30(T - 4) = 10E + 5B + 30T - 25.\n\\]\nThus Ava's score is always exactly 25 points lower than Emma's, independent of the particular values of \\(E\\), \\(B\\), and \\(T\\).\nThe absolute difference between the two scores is therefore 25.\nAnswer: 25", "correct": true, "gold": "25"}
