{"qid": "gsm:111", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "openai/gpt-5.4", "resp": "Let \\(r\\) be the number of red chickens and \\(w\\) the number of white chickens.\n\nWe know:\n- \\(w = r + 2\\)\n- \\(3r + 5w = 42\\)\n\nSubstitute \\(w\\):\n\\[\n3r + 5(r+2) = 42\n\\]\n\\[\n3r + 5r + 10 = 42\n\\]\n\\[\n8r + 10 = 42\n\\]\n\\[\n8r = 32\n\\]\n\\[\nr = 4\n\\]\n\nAnswer: 4", "correct": true, "gold": "4"}
{"qid": "gsm:110", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "Each whale has 40 gallons of blood, so one shark has \\(3 \\times 40 = 120\\) gallons.  \nTen sharks therefore have \\(10 \\times 120 = 1200\\) gallons in total.  \n(The number of whales is irrelevant and is not needed for the calculation.)\n\nAnswer: 1200", "correct": true, "gold": "1200"}
{"qid": "gsm:111", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "DeepSeek-V4-Flash", "resp": "Let \\( r \\) be the number of red chickens and \\( w \\) be the number of white chickens.\n\nWe know:\n- Red chickens produce 3 eggs/day each, white produce 5 eggs/day each.\n- Total eggs per day: \\( 3r + 5w = 42 \\)\n- Two more white than red: \\( w = r + 2 \\)\n\nSubstitute:\n\\[\n3r + 5(r + 2) = 42\n\\]\n\\[\n3r + 5r + 10 = 42\n\\]\n\\[\n8r + 10 = 42\n\\]\n\\[\n8r = 32\n\\]\n\\[\nr = 4\n\\]\n\nAnswer: 4", "correct": true, "gold": "4"}
{"qid": "gsm:111", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "Let $r$ be the number of red chickens and $w$ be the number of white chickens.\n\nFrom the problem:\n- Red chickens produce 3 eggs/day: $3r$ eggs\n- White chickens produce 5 eggs/day: $5w$ eggs\n- Total eggs: $3r + 5w = 42$\n- White chickens exceed red chickens by 2: $w = r + 2$\n\nSubstituting the second equation into the first:\n$$3r + 5(r + 2) = 42$$\n$$3r + 5r + 10 = 42$$\n$$8r = 32$$\n$$r = 4$$\n\nVerification: 4 red chickens produce 12 eggs, and 6 white chickens produce 30 eggs, totaling 42 eggs.\n\nAnswer: 4", "correct": true, "gold": "4"}
{"qid": "gsm:111", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "Let \\( R \\) be the number of red chickens.  \nThen the number of white chickens is \\( W = R + 2 \\).  \n\nThe daily egg equation is  \n\\[ 3R + 5W = 42. \\]  \n\nSubstitute \\( W \\):  \n\\[ 3R + 5(R + 2) = 42 \\]  \n\\[ 3R + 5R + 10 = 42 \\]  \n\\[ 8R = 32 \\]  \n\\[ R = 4. \\]  \n\nVerification: 4 red chickens give \\( 3 \\times 4 = 12 \\) eggs; 6 white chickens give \\( 5 \\times 6 = 30 \\) eggs; total = 42.  \n\nAnswer: 4", "correct": true, "gold": "4"}
{"qid": "gsm:111", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5", "resp": "**Answer: 4**\n\nLet r = number of red chickens, so w = r + 2 white chickens.\n\nEquation: 3r + 5(r + 2) = 42\n\n3r + 5r + 10 = 42\n8r = 32\nr = 4\n\nJerry has **4 red chickens**.\n\nAnswer: 4", "correct": true, "gold": "4"}
{"qid": "gsm:112", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "DeepSeek-V4-Flash", "resp": "Let's break it down step by step:\n\n- Prince Thaddeus slew 100 dragons.\n- Prince Arthur slew three quarters as many as Thaddeus:  \n  \\( \\frac{3}{4} \\times 100 = 75 \\) dragons.\n- Prince Walter slew twice as many as Arthur:  \n  \\( 2 \\times 75 = 150 \\) dragons.\n- Prince Bruce slew one-fifth as many as Walter:  \n  \\( \\frac{1}{5} \\times 150 = 30 \\) dragons.\n\nAnswer: 30", "correct": true, "gold": "30"}
