{"qid": "gsm:111", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Cohere-command-a-plus-05-2026", "resp": "<|START_TEXT|>Let \\(r\\) be the number of red chickens and \\(w\\) the number of white chickens.  \nWe know:\n- Each red chicken lays 3 eggs per day.\n- Each white chicken lays 5 eggs per day.\n- Total eggs collected each day: \\(3r + 5w = 42\\).\n- There are two more white chickens than red chickens: \\(w = r + 2\\).\n\nSubstitute \\(w = r + 2\\) into the egg equation:\n\\[\n3r + 5(r + 2) = 42 \\\\\n3r + 5r + 10 = 42 \\\\\n8r = 32 \\\\\nr = 4.\n\\]\n\nThus, Jerry has **4 red chickens**.\n\nAnswer: 4<|END_TEXT|>", "correct": true, "gold": "4"}
