{"qid": "gsm:114", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "openai/gpt-5.4", "resp": "If Dana skips at 3 mph, and skipping is half as fast as running, then her running speed is:\n\n- Running speed = 6 mph\n\nSince running is four times as fast as walking:\n\n- Walking speed = 6 \u00f7 4 = 1.5 mph\n\nIn 6 hours, she spends:\n\n- One-third running = 2 hours\n- Two-thirds walking = 4 hours\n\nDistance traveled:\n\n- Running: 6 \u00d7 2 = 12 miles\n- Walking: 1.5 \u00d7 4 = 6 miles\n\nTotal distance = 12 + 6 = 18 miles\n\nAnswer: 18 miles", "correct": true, "gold": "18"}
{"qid": "gsm:108", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "DeepSeek-V4-Flash", "resp": "Let\u2019s define the differences:\n\n- Enemies: Ava jumps on 8 more \u2192 +8 \u00d7 10 = +80 points for Ava.\n- Berries: Ava collects 3 more \u2192 +3 \u00d7 5 = +15 points for Ava.\n- Time: Ava finishes 4 seconds slower \u2192 \u22124 \u00d7 30 = \u2212120 points for Ava.\n\nNet difference (Ava \u2212 Emma) = 80 + 15 \u2212 120 = \u221225.\n\nSo Emma scores 25 points more than Ava.\n\nAnswer: 25", "correct": true, "gold": "25"}
{"qid": "gsm:113", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "MAI-Thinking-1", "resp": "He has been vacationing for **34 - 23 = 11 years**. Since he goes on **4 vacations per year**, that gives **11 \u00d7 4 = 44 vacations**. Each vacation shirt is its own quilt block, so he has **44 quilt blocks** in total. \r\n\r\nAnswer: 44", "correct": true, "gold": "44"}
{"qid": "gsm:114", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5", "resp": "Dana's run speed = 2 \u00d7 skip speed = 2 \u00d7 3 = 6 mph\nDana's walk speed = run speed \u00f7 4 = 6 \u00f7 4 = 1.5 mph\n\nRunning time = 1/3 \u00d7 6 hours = 2 hours\nWalking time = 2/3 \u00d7 6 hours = 4 hours\n\nDistance running = 6 mph \u00d7 2 hours = 12 miles\nDistance walking = 1.5 mph \u00d7 4 hours = 6 miles\n\nTotal distance = 12 + 6 = 18 miles\n\nAnswer: 18 miles", "correct": true, "gold": "18"}
{"qid": "gsm:114", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "First, determine Dana's speeds:\n\n- Skipping speed = 3 mph\n- Running speed = 2 \u00d7 skipping speed = 2 \u00d7 3 = **6 mph**\n- Walking speed = running speed \u00f7 4 = 6 \u00f7 4 = **1.5 mph**\n\nNext, calculate the time spent on each activity:\n\n- Total time = 6 hours\n- Running time = \u2153 \u00d7 6 = **2 hours**\n- Walking time = \u2154 \u00d7 6 = **4 hours**\n\nCalculate distances:\n\n- Running distance = 6 mph \u00d7 2 hours = 12 miles\n- Walking distance = 1.5 mph \u00d7 4 hours = 6 miles\n\nTotal distance = 12 + 6 = **18 miles**\n\nAnswer: 18", "correct": true, "gold": "18"}
{"qid": "gsm:114", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "DeepSeek-V4-Flash", "resp": "Let\u2019s break it down step by step.\n\n1. Skipping speed = 3 mph.  \n   Skipping is half as fast as running, so running speed = 2 \u00d7 3 = 6 mph.\n\n2. Running is four times faster than walking, so walking speed = 6 \u00f7 4 = 1.5 mph.\n\n3. Total time = 6 hours.  \n   One-third of time running = 2 hours.  \n   Two-thirds of time walking = 4 hours.\n\n4. Distance running = 6 mph \u00d7 2 h = 12 miles.  \n   Distance walking = 1.5 mph \u00d7 4 h = 6 miles.\n\n5. Total distance = 12 + 6 = 18 miles.\n\nAnswer: 18", "correct": true, "gold": "18"}
{"qid": "gsm:114", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "The problem provides relations between Dana's three speeds but only asks about a journey split between running and walking.  \n\nSkip speed is given as 3 mph.  \nBecause skip speed is defined to be half of run speed, run speed = \\(2 \\times 3 = 6\\) mph.  \nBecause run speed is defined to be four times walk speed, walk speed = \\(6 / 4 = 1.5\\) mph.  \n\nTotal travel time is 6 h.  \nRunning occupies one-third of that time: \\(6 \\times 1/3 = 2\\) h, which covers \\(6 \\times 2 = 12\\) mi.  \nWalking occupies the remaining two-thirds: \\(6 \\times 2/3 = 4\\) h, which covers \\(1.5 \\times 4 = 6\\) mi.  \n\nAdding the two segments yields a total distance of 18 mi.  \n\n(The skip speed is used only to establish the numerical values of the other two speeds; it is not part of the actual journey.)\n\nAnswer: 18", "correct": true, "gold": "18"}
