{"qid": "gsm:118", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "Courtney reported 48, which Kelly claims is 20% higher than the actual attendance.\n\nIf $x$ is the actual number of people, then:\n$$48 = x + 0.20x = 1.20x$$\n\nSolving for $x$:\n$$x = \\frac{48}{1.20} = 40$$\n\nThus, 40 people really attended the concert.\n\nAnswer: 40", "correct": true, "gold": "40"}
{"qid": "gsm:118", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "Courtney reported 48 attendees, but this figure was 20% higher than the true total. Let the actual attendance be \\(x\\). Then:\n\\[\n48 = x \\times 1.2\n\\]\nSolving for \\(x\\):\n\\[\nx = \\frac{48}{1.2} = 40\n\\]\nVerification: 20% of 40 is 8, and \\(40 + 8 = 48\\).\n\nAnswer: 40", "correct": true, "gold": "40"}
{"qid": "gsm:119", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "openai/gpt-5.4", "resp": "Total weekend time: \\(7 + 5 = 12\\) hours.\n\nShe reads for 3 hours, so remaining time is:\n\\(12 - 3 = 9\\) hours.\n\nShe plays video games for \\(\\tfrac{1}{3}\\) of the remaining time:\n\\(\\tfrac{1}{3} \\times 9 = 3\\) hours.\n\nSo soccer time is:\n\\(12 - 3 - 3 = 6\\) hours.\n\nPercentage of the weekend spent playing soccer:\n\\(\\frac{6}{12} \\times 100\\% = 50\\%\\)\n\nAnswer: 50%", "correct": true, "gold": "50"}
