{"qid": "gsm:119", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Cohere-command-a-plus-05-2026", "resp": "<|START_TEXT|>Tatiana has a total of \\(7 + 5 = 12\\) hours in her weekend.  \nShe reads for 3 hours, leaving \\(12 - 3 = 9\\) hours.  \nShe spends \\(\\frac{1}{3}\\) of those 9 hours on video games, which is \\( \\frac{1}{3} \\times 9 = 3\\) hours.  \nThe remaining time for soccer is \\(9 - 3 = 6\\) hours.  \n\nThe percentage of her weekend spent playing soccer is:\n\\[\n\\frac{6\\text{ hours}}{12\\text{ hours}} \\times 100\\% = 50\\%\n\\]\n\nAnswer: 50%<|END_TEXT|>", "correct": true, "gold": "50"}
{"qid": "gsm:120", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "openai/gpt-5.4", "resp": "The car loses 21% of its value each year, so it keeps 79% of its value annually.\n\nFrom 2007 to 2010 is 3 years, so:\n\n\\[\n20000(0.79)^3\n\\]\n\n\\[\n20000(0.79)^3 = 20000(0.493039) = 9860.78\n\\]\n\nSo the price of the car in 2010 is **$9,860.78**.\n\nAnswer: $9,860.78", "correct": false, "gold": "7400"}
{"qid": "gsm:120", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "DeepSeek-V4-Flash", "resp": "We know the car's initial value is $20,000 in 2007, and it depreciates at 21% per year.  \nDepreciation of 21% per year means the car retains \\( 100\\% - 21\\% = 79\\% \\) of its value each year.  \nSo the multiplier each year is 0.79.\n\nFrom 2007 to 2010 is 3 years.\n\nThe price in 2010 is:\n\\[\n20000 \\times (0.79)^3\n\\]\n\nFirst, \\(0.79^2 = 0.6241\\).  \nThen \\(0.6241 \\times 0.79 = 0.493039\\).\n\nNow multiply by 20000:\n\\[\n20000 \\times 0.493039 = 9860.78\n\\]\n\nSo the price in 2010 is $9860.78.\n\nAnswer: $9860.78", "correct": false, "gold": "7400"}
{"qid": "gsm:119", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "DeepSeek-V4-Flash", "resp": "Let\u2019s break it down step by step.\n\nTotal weekend hours:  \nSaturday: 7 hours  \nSunday: 5 hours  \nTotal = 7 + 5 = 12 hours  \n\nShe reads for 3 hours:  \nRemaining time = 12 \u2013 3 = 9 hours  \n\nShe plays video games for 1/3 of the remaining time:  \nVideo games = (1/3) \u00d7 9 = 3 hours  \n\nTime left for soccer = 9 \u2013 3 = 6 hours  \n\nPercentage of weekend spent on soccer:  \n(6 / 12) \u00d7 100% = 50%  \n\nAnswer: 50%", "correct": true, "gold": "50"}
{"qid": "gsm:120", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5", "resp": "**Setting up the depreciation formula:**\n\nPrice = Initial Price \u00d7 (1 - rate)^years\n\n- Initial Price = $20,000\n- Rate = 21% = 0.21\n- Years = 2010 - 2007 = 3\n\n**Calculating:**\n\nPrice = 20000 \u00d7 (1 - 0.21)^3\nPrice = 20000 \u00d7 (0.79)^3\nPrice = 20000 \u00d7 0.493039\nPrice = $9,860.78\n\nAnswer: $9,860.78", "correct": false, "gold": "7400"}
{"qid": "gsm:119", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "Total weekend time is 7 + 5 = 12 hours.\nAfter 3 hours of reading, 9 hours remain.\nVideo games take 1/3 of those 9 hours = 3 hours.\nThis leaves 6 hours for soccer.\nThus (6/12) * 100 = 50.\nAnswer: 50", "correct": true, "gold": "50"}
{"qid": "gsm:121", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "openai/gpt-5.4", "resp": "Half of 2 bolts is 1 bolt, so the robe uses:\n\n- 2 bolts of blue fiber\n- 1 bolt of white fiber\n\nTotal: 2 + 1 = 3 bolts\n\nAnswer: 3 bolts", "correct": true, "gold": "3"}
