{"qid": "gsm:122", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "openai/gpt-5.4", "resp": "Let \\(y\\) be the number of yellow balloons.\n\nBenny threw:\n- \\(2\\) pieces at each of \\(20\\) red balloons: \\(2 \\cdot 20 = 40\\)\n- \\(3\\) pieces at each yellow balloon: \\(3y\\)\n\nTotal pieces thrown was \\(58\\), so:\n\n\\[\n40 + 3y = 58\n\\]\n\n\\[\n3y = 18\n\\]\n\n\\[\ny = 6\n\\]\n\nAnswer: 6", "correct": true, "gold": "6"}
{"qid": "gsm:120", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "The car depreciates by 21% per year, meaning it retains 79% (or 0.79) of its value annually.\n\nFrom 2007 to 2010 is 3 years.\n\nUsing the depreciation formula:  \nFinal Price = Initial Price \u00d7 (1 \u2212 Rate)$^{Time}$\n\nFinal Price = $20,000 \u00d7 (0.79)^3$  \nFinal Price = $20,000 \u00d7 0.493039$  \nFinal Price = $9,860.78$\n\nAnswer: $9860.78 (or approximately $9861)", "correct": false, "gold": "7400"}
{"qid": "gsm:122", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "DeepSeek-V4-Flash", "resp": "Let \\( r \\) be the number of red balloons and \\( y \\) be the number of yellow balloons.  \nWe know \\( r = 20 \\).  \nEach red balloon gets 2 pieces of bologna, each yellow gets 3 pieces.  \nTotal bologna:  \n\\[\n2r + 3y = 58\n\\]  \nSubstitute \\( r = 20 \\):  \n\\[\n2(20) + 3y = 58\n\\]  \n\\[\n40 + 3y = 58\n\\]  \n\\[\n3y = 18\n\\]  \n\\[\ny = 6\n\\]  \n\nAnswer: 6", "correct": true, "gold": "6"}
{"qid": "gsm:122", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "Let $r$ be the number of red balloons and $y$ be the number of yellow balloons.\n\nFrom the problem:\n- $r = 20$\n- Each red balloon gets 2 pieces: $2r$ pieces total\n- Each yellow balloon gets 3 pieces: $3y$ pieces total\n- Total pieces thrown: $58$\n\nEquation: $2r + 3y = 58$\n\nSubstitute $r = 20$:\n$$2(20) + 3y = 58$$\n$$40 + 3y = 58$$\n$$3y = 18$$\n$$y = 6$$\n\nCheck: $20$ red balloons $\\times$ $2$ pieces = $40$ pieces, and $6$ yellow balloons $\\times$ $3$ pieces = $18$ pieces. $40 + 18 = 58$.\n\nAnswer: 6", "correct": true, "gold": "6"}
{"qid": "gsm:122", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5", "resp": "**Answer: 6**\n\nReasoning: Benny threw 2 pieces per red balloon, so 20 red balloons used 20 \u00d7 2 = 40 pieces of bologna. That leaves 58 \u2212 40 = 18 pieces for yellow balloons, at 3 pieces each: 18 \u00f7 3 = 6 yellow balloons.\n\nAnswer: 6", "correct": true, "gold": "6"}
{"qid": "gsm:122", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "Let \\( R \\) be red balloons and \\( Y \\) yellow balloons.  \nGiven \\( R = 20 \\) and total bologna pieces satisfy \\( 2R + 3Y = 58 \\).  \nSubstitute: \\( 2(20) + 3Y = 58 \\).  \nSimplify: \\( 40 + 3Y = 58 \\).  \nSolve: \\( 3Y = 18 \\), so \\( Y = 6 \\).  \n\nAnswer: 6", "correct": true, "gold": "6"}
{"qid": "gsm:123", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "openai/gpt-5.4", "resp": "Bob needs 56 popsicle sticks.\n\nEach box has 8 sticks, so:\n56 \u00f7 8 = 7 boxes\n\nEach box costs $2.00, so:\n7 \u00d7 $2.00 = $14.00\n\nAnswer: $14.00", "correct": true, "gold": "14"}
{"qid": "gsm:123", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "DeepSeek-V4-Flash", "resp": "We need to find out how many boxes Bob must buy to get at least 56 sticks.  \n\nEach box has 8 sticks.  \n56 \u00f7 8 = 7 boxes exactly.  \n\nEach box costs $2.00.  \n7 \u00d7 $2.00 = $14.00.  \n\nAnswer: $14.00", "correct": true, "gold": "14"}
{"qid": "gsm:122", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Cohere-command-a-plus-05-2026", "resp": "<|START_TEXT|>Benny threw 2 pieces of bologna at each red balloon and 3 pieces at each yellow balloon.  \nLet \\(R\\) be the number of red balloons (given as 20) and \\(Y\\) be the number of yellow balloons.  \n\nThe total pieces of bologna thrown is:\n\\[\n2R + 3Y = 58\n\\]\n\nSubstituting \\(R = 20\\):\n\\[\n2(20) + 3Y = 58 \\\\\n40 + 3Y = 58 \\\\\n3Y = 18 \\\\\nY = 6\n\\]\n\nSo there were 6 yellow balloons in the bundle.\n\nAnswer: 6<|END_TEXT|>", "correct": true, "gold": "6"}
{"qid": "gsm:123", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "Bob needs 56 popsicle sticks, and each box contains 8 sticks, so he needs $56 \\div 8 = 7$ boxes. At $\\$2.00$ per box, the total cost is $7 \\times \\$2.00 = \\$14.00$.\n\nAnswer: $14.00", "correct": true, "gold": "14"}
{"qid": "gsm:120", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "The value of the car follows the exponential decay model \\(A = P(1 - r)^t\\), where \\(P = 20000\\) is the initial price, \\(r = 0.21\\) is the annual depreciation rate, and \\(t = 3\\) is the number of years from 2007 to 2010. Substituting the values gives  \n\\[\nA = 20000 \\times (0.79)^3.\n\\]  \nFirst compute the power:  \n\\[\n0.79^2 = 0.6241, \\qquad 0.6241 \\times 0.79 = 0.493039.\n\\]  \nThen multiply by the initial price:  \n\\[\n20000 \\times 0.493039 = 9860.78.\n\\]  \nThus the price in 2010 is \\(9860.78\\) dollars (to the nearest cent).  \n\nAnswer: $9860.78", "correct": false, "gold": "7400"}
