{"qid": "gsm:127", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "openai/gpt-5.4", "resp": "Each paid scoop costs $1.50, and the deal is \u201cbuy 2, get 1 free.\u201d\n\nWith $6.00, Erin can pay for:\n\n- $6.00 \u00f7 $1.50 = 4 paid scoops\n\nFor every 2 scoops she buys, she gets 1 free:\n\n- 4 paid scoops gives 2 free scoops\n\nSo total scoops:\n\n- 4 + 2 = 6 scoops\n\nAnswer: 6 scoops", "correct": true, "gold": "6"}
{"qid": "gsm:127", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "DeepSeek-V4-Flash", "resp": "Erin has $6.00, and each scoop costs $1.50.  \nWithout the deal, she could buy $6.00 \u00f7 $1.50 = 4 scoops.  \n\nWith the deal \"buy 2, get 1 free\":  \n- If she buys 2 scoops ($3.00), she gets 1 free \u2192 total 3 scoops.  \n- If she buys 4 scoops ($6.00), she gets 2 free (since she qualifies for two sets of the deal) \u2192 total 6 scoops.  \n\nSo with $6.00, she should buy 4 scoops (paying for 4) and get 2 free, ending with 6 scoops.\n\nAnswer: 6", "correct": true, "gold": "6"}
{"qid": "gsm:126", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Cohere-command-a-plus-05-2026", "resp": "<|START_TEXT|>Elise started with 250 books and has 50 left unsold, so she has sold 250\u202f\u2212\u202f50\u202f=\u202f200 books over three years.  \nShe sold 45 books this (the third) year. The first year\u2019s sales were twice the current year\u2019s sales: 2\u202f\u00d7\u202f45\u202f=\u202f90 books.  \n\nThus, the second year's sales = total sold\u202f\u2212\u202f(first year\u202f+\u202fthird year) = 200\u202f\u2212\u202f(90\u202f+\u202f45) = 65 books.  \n\nEach book sells for $20, so the second\u2011year earnings = 65\u202f\u00d7\u202f$20 = $1,300.  \n\nAnswer: $1300<|END_TEXT|>", "correct": true, "gold": "1300"}
