{"qid": "gsm:126", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "The total number of books sold across all three years is \\(250 - 50 = 200\\).\n\nLet \\(C\\) be the number sold in the current (third) year. The problem states that this equals 45, so \\(C = 45\\).\n\nThe first-year sales \\(A\\) satisfy \\(A = 2C = 90\\).\n\nLet \\(B\\) be the number sold in the second year. Then:\n\\[\n90 + B + 45 = 200 \\implies B = 65.\n\\]\n\nRevenue in the second year is therefore \\(65 \\times 20 = 1300\\).\n\nAll quantities are consistent with the given totals and constraints; no information is contradictory or superfluous.\n\nAnswer: 1300", "correct": true, "gold": "1300"}
{"qid": "gsm:128", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "DeepSeek-V4-Flash", "resp": "Let's break it down:\n\n- A small sunflower has 3 dozen seeds.  \n  3 dozen = 3 \u00d7 12 = 36 seeds.\n\n- A large sunflower has 50% more seeds than a small sunflower.  \n  50% more means 36 + (0.5 \u00d7 36) = 36 + 18 = 54 seeds.\n\n- Altogether, one small and one large sunflower have:  \n  36 + 54 = 90 seeds.\n\nAnswer: 90", "correct": true, "gold": "90"}
