{"qid": "gsm:135", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "openai/gpt-5.4", "resp": "Let \\(x\\) be the number of cards Kenny started with.\n\nHe keeps \\(\\tfrac{1}{3}\\) of them, so he sells \\(\\tfrac{2}{3}x\\) cards.\n\nEach sold card brings in \\$1.50, so the money he makes is:\n\n\\[\n1.5 \\cdot \\frac{2}{3}x = x\n\\]\n\nHe needs enough for:\n- \\$100 for the ticket\n- \\$50 spending cash\n\nSo he needs \\$150 total.\n\nSince the money from selling the cards equals \\(x\\), we get:\n\n\\[\nx = 150\n\\]\n\nAnswer: 150", "correct": true, "gold": "150"}
{"qid": "gsm:134", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "Each room has:\n- 2 sheets\n- 1 comforter\n- pillow cases = 2 \u00d7 sheets = 4\n- towels = 2 \u00d7 pillow cases = 8\n\nThis gives a total of 2 + 1 + 4 + 8 = 15 pieces per room.\n\nFor 80 rooms the total is therefore 80 \u00d7 15 = 1200.\n\n(Equivalently, across all rooms there are 160 sheets, 80 comforters, 320 pillow cases and 640 towels, which again sum to 1200.)\n\nAnswer: 1200", "correct": true, "gold": "1200"}
{"qid": "gsm:135", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "Let $x$ be the number of cards Kenny started with.\n\nHe keeps $\\frac{1}{3}$ of them, so he sells $\\frac{2}{3}x$ cards.\n\nAt $\\$1.5$ per card, his revenue is:\n$$\\frac{2}{3}x \\times \\$1.5 = \\$150$$\n\nThis is because he needs $\\$100$ for the ticket plus $\\$50$ spending cash.\n\nSolving:\n$$\\frac{2}{3}x \\times 1.5 = 150$$\n$$\\frac{2}{3}x \\times \\frac{3}{2} = 150$$\n$$x = 150$$\n\nVerification: With 150 cards, he sells 100 cards (keeping 50). At $\\$1.5$ each, he earns $\\$150$. After buying the $\\$100$ ticket, he has $\\$50$ left.\n\nAnswer: 150", "correct": true, "gold": "150"}
{"qid": "gsm:135", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5", "resp": "He needs $100 for the ticket plus $50 spending cash, so total money from selling cards = $150.\n\nHe sells 2/3 of his cards (since he keeps 1/3), each at $1.5:\n\n(2/3)N \u00d7 1.5 = 150\nN \u00d7 1 = 150\nN = 150\n\nAnswer: 150", "correct": true, "gold": "150"}
{"qid": "gsm:135", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "DeepSeek-V4-Flash", "resp": "We know Kenny ends up with $50 spending cash after buying the $100 ticket, so he must have made $150 total from selling cards.\n\nLet the total number of cards be \\( x \\).  \nHe keeps \\( \\frac{1}{3}x \\), so he sells \\( \\frac{2}{3}x \\) cards.  \nEach card sells for $1.5, so his earnings are:\n\n\\[\n1.5 \\times \\frac{2}{3}x = x\n\\]\n\nThus, his earnings equal \\( x \\) dollars.  \nWe know he earned $150, so:\n\n\\[\nx = 150\n\\]\n\nAnswer: 150", "correct": true, "gold": "150"}
{"qid": "gsm:133", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Cohere-command-a-plus-05-2026", "resp": "<|START_TEXT|>James rents the carriage for 4 hours (5\u20119\u202fPM) but gets 1 hour free, so he pays for 3 hours.  \n- First paid hour: \\$15  \n- Each additional paid hour costs twice the first hour\u2019s cost: 2\u202f\u00d7\u202f\\$15 = \\$30 per hour  \n\nTotal cost = \\$15 + \\$30 + \\$30 = \\$75.  \n\nAnswer: $75<|END_TEXT|>", "correct": true, "gold": "75"}
{"qid": "gsm:132", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "The new device adds 2 kilowatt-hours (kWh) of consumption per day. Over one week (7 days), this adds:\n\n$$2 \\text{ kWh/day} \\times 7 \\text{ days} = 14 \\text{ kWh}$$\n\nAt a rate of $\\$1.50$ per kWh, the additional weekly cost is:\n\n$$14 \\text{ kWh} \\times \\$1.50/\\text{kWh} = \\$21$$\n\nThus, the difference between the weekly bills is $\\$21$.\n\nAnswer: $21$", "correct": true, "gold": "21"}
{"qid": "gsm:134", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "MAI-Thinking-1", "resp": "Each room has: \r\n\r\n- 2 sheets\r\n- 1 comforter\r\n- 4 pillow cases (twice as many as sheets: 2 \u00d7 2)\r\n- 8 towels (twice as many as pillow cases: 2 \u00d7 4)\r\n\r\nTotal per room = 2 + 1 + 4 + 8 = 15 pieces.\r\n\r\nFor 80 rooms: 15 \u00d7 80 = 1200 pieces.\r\n\r\nAnswer: 1200", "correct": true, "gold": "1200"}
