{"qid": "gsm:139", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "The ratio of men to women is given as 5:9, and their combined total is 84 passengers. This means the parts in the ratio add up to 14, so each part represents \\(84 / 14 = 6\\) passengers.\n\nMultiplying through the ratio then gives:\n- Men: \\(5 \\times 6 = 30\\)\n- Women: \\(9 \\times 6 = 54\\)\n\nAfter 20 women leave the bus, the number of women remaining is \\(54 - 20 = 34\\).\n\nAnswer: 34", "correct": true, "gold": "34"}
{"qid": "gsm:137", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "DeepSeek-V4-Flash", "resp": "We know Ana peels an orange in 3 minutes, so in 60 minutes she peels:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{60}{3} = 20 \\text{ oranges}\n\\]\n\nJane peels an orange in 4 minutes, so in 60 minutes she peels:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{60}{4} = 15 \\text{ oranges}\n\\]\n\nThe difference is:\n\n\\[\n20 - 15 = 5\n\\]\n\nAnswer: 5", "correct": true, "gold": "5"}
