{"qid": "gsm:154", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5", "resp": "**Distance calculation:**\n\n- Leg 1 (south): 10 hours \u00d7 30 mph = 300 miles south\n- Leg 2 (north): 2 hours \u00d7 18 mph = 36 miles north\n- Leg 3 (south): 5 hours \u00d7 22 mph = 110 miles south\n\n**Net distance south** = 300 \u2212 36 + 110 = 374 miles\n\nAnswer: 374", "correct": true, "gold": "374"}
{"qid": "gsm:154", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "DeepSeek-V4-Flash", "resp": "We need to find the net displacement from start to finish.  \n\nFirst leg: south for 10 hours at 30 mph \u2192 distance south = 10 \u00d7 30 = 300 miles south.  \nSecond leg: north for 2 hours at 18 mph \u2192 distance north = 2 \u00d7 18 = 36 miles north.  \nThird leg: south for 5 hours at 22 mph \u2192 distance south = 5 \u00d7 22 = 110 miles south.  \n\nNet southward distance = 300 - 36 + 110 = 374 miles.  \n\nAnswer: 374", "correct": true, "gold": "374"}
{"qid": "gsm:154", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Cohere-command-a-plus-05-2026", "resp": "<|START_TEXT|>The bird's total southward displacement is the sum of the southward distances minus the northward segment:\n\n- Southward leg 1: \\(10 \\text{ hr} \\times 30 \\text{ mph} = 300\\) miles south  \n- Northward leg: \\(2 \\text{ hr} \\times 18 \\text{ mph} = 36\\) miles north  \n- Southward leg 2: \\(5 \\text{ hr} \\times 22 \\text{ mph} = 110\\) miles south  \n\nNet displacement south = \\(300 + 110 - 36 = 374\\) miles.\n\nAnswer: 374<|END_TEXT|>", "correct": true, "gold": "374"}
{"qid": "gsm:155", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "openai/gpt-5.4", "resp": "Let Colin\u2019s current age be \\(c\\) and Wendy\u2019s current age be \\(w\\).\n\nFrom \u201cWendy is five times as old as Colin will be seven years from now\u201d:\n\\[\nw = 5(c+7)\n\\]\n\nFrom \u201cIn 25 years, Colin will be a third as old as Wendy is now\u201d:\n\\[\nc+25 = \\frac{1}{3}w\n\\]\n\nSubstitute \\(w = 3(c+25)\\) into the first equation:\n\\[\n3(c+25) = 5(c+7)\n\\]\n\nExpand:\n\\[\n3c + 75 = 5c + 35\n\\]\n\n\\[\n40 = 2c\n\\]\n\n\\[\nc = 20\n\\]\n\nAnswer: 20", "correct": true, "gold": "20"}
{"qid": "gsm:154", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "The bird's journey consists of three legs:\n\n1. **South for 10 hours at 30 mph:** $10 \\times 30 = 300$ miles south\n2. **North for 2 hours at 18 mph:** $2 \\times 18 = 36$ miles north  \n3. **South for 5 hours at 22 mph:** $5 \\times 22 = 110$ miles south\n\nTo find the distance between the two homes, calculate the net displacement from the starting point:\n\n$$300 - 36 + 110 = 374\\text{ miles south}$$\n\nSince the bird lands at her southern home after this journey, the distance between the northern and southern homes is 374 miles.\n\nAnswer: 374", "correct": true, "gold": "374"}
{"qid": "gsm:154", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "The bird's journey consists of three legs, with only north-south motion mentioned. Define the north home as position 0 and treat south as the positive direction. The net displacement after all three legs is then the distance separating the two homes.\n- First leg (south): \\(10 \\times 30 = +300\\) miles.\n- Second leg (north): \\(2 \\times 18 = -36\\) miles.\n- Third leg (south): \\(5 \\times 22 = +110\\) miles.\nAdding these displacements yields the final position:\n\\[\n300 - 36 + 110 = 374.\n\\]\nBecause the bird lands at the southern home, that home lies 374 miles south of the northern home.\nAnswer: 374", "correct": true, "gold": "374"}
{"qid": "gsm:155", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "DeepSeek-V4-Flash", "resp": "Let Colin's current age be \\( c \\) and Wendy's current age be \\( w \\).\n\n**First statement:**  \n\"Wendy is five times as old as Colin will be seven years from now.\"  \nColin in 7 years: \\( c + 7 \\)  \nSo:  \n\\[\nw = 5(c + 7)\n\\]\n\n**Second statement:**  \n\"In 25 years, Colin will be a third as old as Wendy is now.\"  \nColin in 25 years: \\( c + 25 \\)  \nWendy now: \\( w \\)  \nSo:  \n\\[\nc + 25 = \\frac{1}{3} w\n\\]\n\nNow substitute \\( w = 5(c + 7) \\) into the second equation:  \n\\[\nc + 25 = \\frac{1}{3} \\cdot 5(c + 7)\n\\]  \n\\[\nc + 25 = \\frac{5}{3}(c + 7)\n\\]  \nMultiply both sides by 3:  \n\\[\n3c + 75 = 5(c + 7)\n\\]  \n\\[\n3c + 75 = 5c + 35\n\\]  \n\\[\n75 - 35 = 5c - 3c\n\\]  \n\\[\n40 = 2c\n\\]  \n\\[\nc = 20\n\\]\n\nAnswer: 20", "correct": true, "gold": "20"}
{"qid": "gsm:154", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "MAI-Thinking-1", "resp": "Answer: 374 miles", "correct": true, "gold": "374"}
{"qid": "gsm:152", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "DeepSeek-V4-Flash", "resp": "First, find the cost to repave Monica's street:  \n150 meters \u00d7 $194/meter = $29,100.\n\nNext, find the cost to repave Lewis' street:  \n490 meters \u00d7 $194/meter = $95,060.\n\nThen, find the difference:  \n$95,060 \u2212 $29,100 = $65,960.\n\nAnswer: $65,960", "correct": true, "gold": "65960"}
{"qid": "gsm:155", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5", "resp": "**Setting up equations:**\n\nLet W = Wendy's current age, C = Colin's current age.\n\n- \"Wendy is five times as old as Colin will be seven years from now\":\n  W = 5(C + 7)\n\n- \"In 25 years, Colin will be a third as old as Wendy is now\":\n  C + 25 = W/3\n\n**Solving the system:**\n\nFrom the first equation: W = 5C + 35\n\nSubstitute into the second equation:\nC + 25 = (5C + 35)/3\n\nMultiply both sides by 3:\n3C + 75 = 5C + 35\n\n75 \u2212 35 = 5C \u2212 3C\n40 = 2C\nC = 20\n\n**Check:** \n- Wendy's age: W = 5(20+7) = 5(27) = 135\n- In 25 years, Colin will be 45, and W/3 = 135/3 = 45 \u2713\n\nAnswer: 20", "correct": true, "gold": "20"}
{"qid": "gsm:156", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "DeepSeek-V4-Flash", "resp": "We know Comet Halley returns every 75 years.  \n\nLet Bill's dad's age when he saw the comet = 30.  \nBill saw the comet a second time when he was three times that age:  \n3 \u00d7 30 = 90 years old.  \n\nSince the comet returns every 75 years, the first time Bill saw it was 75 years before his second sighting:  \n90 \u2212 75 = 15 years old.  \n\nAnswer: 15", "correct": true, "gold": "15"}
{"qid": "gsm:156", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "openai/gpt-5.4", "resp": "Halley\u2019s Comet appears every 75 years.\n\nBill\u2019s dad saw it when he was 30.\n\nBill saw it the **second** time when he was **three times** his father\u2019s age at that sighting:\n\n- \\(3 \\times 30 = 90\\)\n\nSo Bill was **90** the second time he saw the comet.\n\nSince sightings are 75 years apart, Bill\u2019s first sighting was:\n\n- \\(90 - 75 = 15\\)\n\nAnswer: 15", "correct": true, "gold": "15"}
{"qid": "gsm:155", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "Let \\(C\\) be Colin's current age and \\(W\\) be Wendy's current age.\n\nThe first statement gives the equation  \n\\[W = 5(C + 7).\\]\n\nThe second statement gives the equation  \n\\[C + 25 = \\frac{W}{3}.\\]\n\nSubstitute \\(W = 5C + 35\\) into the second equation:  \n\\[C + 25 = \\frac{5C + 35}{3}.\\]  \n\nMultiply through by 3:  \n\\[3C + 75 = 5C + 35.\\]  \n\nRearrange:  \n\\[40 = 2C,\\]  \nso  \n\\[C = 20.\\]  \n\n(The corresponding value of \\(W\\) is 135, which satisfies both original statements.)\n\nAnswer: 20", "correct": true, "gold": "20"}
{"qid": "gsm:155", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Cohere-command-a-plus-05-2026", "resp": "<|START_TEXT|>Answer: 20<|END_TEXT|>", "correct": true, "gold": "20"}
{"qid": "gsm:155", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "Let $C$ be Colin's current age and $W$ be Wendy's current age.\n\nFrom the first statement: $W = 5(C + 7) = 5C + 35$\n\nFrom the second statement: $C + 25 = \\frac{1}{3}W$\n\nSubstituting the first equation into the second:\n$$C + 25 = \\frac{1}{3}(5C + 35)$$\n\nMultiplying by 3:\n$$3C + 75 = 5C + 35$$\n$$40 = 2C$$\n$$C = 20$$\n\nVerification: If Colin is 20, in 7 years he will be 27, making Wendy $5 \\times 27 = 135$. In 25 years, Colin will be 45, which is indeed $\\frac{1}{3}$ of 135.\n\nAnswer: 20", "correct": true, "gold": "20"}
{"qid": "gsm:157", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "openai/gpt-5.4", "resp": "One son is 12. The other is 4 years younger, so he is 8.\n\nTotal candles needed: 12 + 8 = 20\n\nCandles come in packs of 5, so James needs:\n20 \u00f7 5 = 4 packs\n\nEach pack costs $3, so total cost is:\n4 \u00d7 3 = $12\n\nAnswer: $12", "correct": true, "gold": "12"}
{"qid": "gsm:156", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5", "resp": "Bill saw the comet when he was **15 years old**.\n\nReasoning: Bill's dad saw the comet at age 30. Bill saw it \"a second time\" at 3\u00d7 that age = 90 years old. Since the comet returns every 75 years, the previous appearance (Bill's first sighting) was 75 years before he turned 90, i.e., at age 90 \u2212 75 = 15.\n\nAnswer: 15", "correct": true, "gold": "15"}
