{"qid": "gsm:156", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "The comet appears every 75 years, so any two sightings by Bill are separated by a multiple of 75 years. The problem states that Bill was 90 years old at his second sighting (three times his father's age of 30 at the father's sighting).  \n\nTo yield a unique numerical answer, the father's sighting must coincide with Bill's first sighting (otherwise the problem supplies insufficient information about Bill's birth year to relate the two timelines). This places the two sightings exactly 75 years apart, so Bill's age at the first sighting is \\(90 - 75 = 15\\).  \n\n(The implied paternal age of 15 at Bill's birth is biologically possible and does not contradict any stated fact.)\n\nAnswer: 15", "correct": true, "gold": "15"}
