{"qid": "gsm:161", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "openai/gpt-5.4", "resp": "100 books cost $500, so each book costs:\n\n\\[\n500 \\div 100 = 5\n\\]\n\nSo with $27{,}000, Bob can buy:\n\n\\[\n27000 \\div 5 = 5400 \\text{ books}\n\\]\n\nDistributed equally among 3 schools:\n\n\\[\n5400 \\div 3 = 1800\n\\]\n\nAnswer: 1800 books per school", "correct": true, "gold": "1800"}
{"qid": "gsm:161", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "First, find the cost per book: $\\$500 \\div 100 = \\$5$ per book.\n\nNext, find the total number of books: $\\$27{,}000 \\div \\$5 = 5{,}400$ books.\n\nFinally, divide by 3 schools: $5{,}400 \\div 3 = 1{,}800$ books per school.\n\n(Alternatively: $\\$27{,}000 \\div 3 = \\$9{,}000$ per school. At $\\$500$ per 100 books, $\\$9{,}000$ buys $18 \\times 100 = 1{,}800$ books.)\n\nAnswer: 1800", "correct": true, "gold": "1800"}
