{"qid": "gsm:161", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "Total expenditure is $27000 for books across 3 schools.  \nBooks are purchased at a rate of 100 for $500, or equivalently $5 per book.  \nThis yields a total of \\(27000 \\div 5 = 5400\\) books.  \nAssuming equal distribution across the schools gives \\(5400 \\div 3 = 1800\\) books per school.  \n(Equivalently: \\(27000 \\div 3 = 9000\\) dollars per school, then \\(9000 \\div 500 \\times 100 = 1800\\).)\n\nAnswer: 1800", "correct": true, "gold": "1800"}
