{"qid": "gsm:156", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Cohere-command-a-plus-05-2026", "resp": "<|START_TEXT|>Bill\u2019s second sighting occurs at age\u202f\\(3\\times30 = 90\\).  \nSince Halley\u2019s comet returns every 75\u202fyears, the time between Bill\u2019s first and second sightings must be a multiple of 75.  \n\nLet \\(k\\) be the number of comet cycles between his first and second viewings.  \nThen  \n\\[\n\\text{age at first sighting} + 75k = 90.\n\\]\n\nThe only non\u2011negative integer solution is \\(k=1\\), giving  \n\\[\n\\text{age at first sighting}=90-75=15.\n\\]\n\nThis also fits the family timeline: if Bill first saw the comet at age\u202f15, his father\u2014who saw it at age\u202f30\u2014would be 15\u202fyears older, making the age gap realistic (father had Bill at age\u202f15).  \n\nAnswer: 15.<|END_TEXT|>", "correct": true, "gold": "15"}
