{"qid": "gsm:167", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Cohere-command-a-plus-05-2026", "resp": "<|START_TEXT|>Emily\u2019s children satisfy the following age relations:\n\n- Let \\(A\\) = Amy\u2019s age, \\(J\\) = Jackson\u2019s age, \\(C\\) = Corey\u2019s age, and \\(M\\) = James\u2019s age.\n- \\(A = J + 5\\)\u2003(Amy is 5 years older than Jackson)\n- \\(A = C - 2\\)\u2003(Amy is 2 years younger than Corey)\n- \\(M = 10\\) and \\(M = C - 1\\)\u2003(James is 1 year younger than Corey)\n\nFrom \\(M = C - 1\\):  \n\\(C = M + 1 = 10 + 1 = 11\\).\n\nFrom \\(A = C - 2\\):  \n\\(A = 11 - 2 = 9\\).\n\nFrom \\(A = J + 5\\):  \n\\(J = A - 5 = 9 - 5 = 4\\).\n\nThus Jackson is 4 years old.\n\nAnswer: 4<|END_TEXT|>", "correct": true, "gold": "4"}
