{"qid": "gsm:176", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Cohere-command-a-plus-05-2026", "resp": "<|START_TEXT|>Martha invited \\(2\\) families of \\(6\\) people each and \\(3\\) families of \\(4\\) people each:\n\n\\[\n2 \\times 6 + 3 \\times 4 = 12 + 12 = 24 \\text{ invited guests}\n\\]\n\nEight guests couldn\u2019t attend due to illness. Additionally, \\(\\frac{1}{4}\\) of that number (i.e., \\(\\frac{1}{4}\\times 8 = 2\\)) had previous commitments, meaning they also could not attend.  \n\nTotal absent guests:\n\n\\[\n8 + 2 = 10\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the number of people who actually show up is:\n\n\\[\n24 - 10 = 14\n\\]\n\nAnswer: 14<|END_TEXT|>", "correct": true, "gold": "14"}
