{"qid": "gsm:184", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "MAI-Thinking-1", "resp": "**Reasoning:**\n\n1. **First Leg:** John drives for 3 hours at 60 mph.  \n   Distance = 3 \u00d7 60 = 180 miles away from home.\n\n2. **Return Trip (4 hours total):**\n   - **First 2 hours:** Standstill traffic \u2192 Distance = 0 miles.\n   - **Next 0.5 hours:** Driving at 30 mph \u2192 Distance = 0.5 \u00d7 30 = 15 miles toward home.\n   - **Remaining time:** 4 - 2 - 0.5 = 1.5 hours at 80 mph \u2192 Distance = 1.5 \u00d7 80 = 120 miles toward home.\n   \n   Total distance traveled back = 0 + 15 + 120 = 135 miles.\n\n3. **Final Distance from Home:** 180 miles (outward) - 135 miles (back) = 45 miles.\n\nAnswer: 45 miles", "correct": true, "gold": "45"}
