{"qid": "gsm:184", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "DeepSeek-V4-Flash", "resp": "Let\u2019s break it down step by step.\n\n1. **First leg:**  \nJohn drives for 3 hours at 60 mph.  \nDistance from home = \\( 3 \\times 60 = 120 \\) miles away.\n\n2. **Turn around and head home:**  \nHe wants to get home in 4 hours total for the return.\n\n3. **First 2 hours of return:**  \nStandstill traffic \u2192 0 miles covered.\n\n4. **Next 0.5 hours:**  \nSpeed = 30 mph \u2192 distance = \\( 0.5 \\times 30 = 15 \\) miles toward home.\n\n5. **Remaining time of the 4 hours:**  \nTotal return time = 4 hours.  \nTime used so far = 2 + 0.5 = 2.5 hours.  \nRemaining time = 4 - 2.5 = 1.5 hours at 80 mph.  \nDistance = \\( 1.5 \\times 80 = 120 \\) miles toward home.\n\n6. **Total distance covered toward home:**  \n15 + 120 = 135 miles.\n\n7. **Distance from home:**  \nHe started 120 miles away, drove 135 miles toward home.  \nSince 135 > 120, he overshoots home by \\( 135 - 120 = 15 \\) miles in the opposite direction.\n\nSo at the end, he is 15 miles from home.\n\nAnswer: 15", "correct": false, "gold": "45"}
