{"qid": "gsm:193", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "openai/gpt-5.4", "resp": "Each CD normally costs $15, so 10 CDs would cost:\n\n10 \u00d7 15 = 150\n\nHe gets 40% off, so he pays 60% of the original price:\n\n150 \u00d7 0.6 = 90\n\nSo James spent $90 total.\n\nHe sells 5 of them for $40 total, so he gets back $40.\n\nMoney he was out:\n\n90 - 40 = 50\n\nAnswer: $50", "correct": true, "gold": "50"}
{"qid": "gsm:193", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "DeepSeek-V4-Flash", "resp": "Let's break it down step by step.\n\n1. **Cost of CDs before discount**:  \n   10 CDs \u00d7 $15 = $150.\n\n2. **Discount**: 40% off means he pays 60% of the price.  \n   $150 \u00d7 0.60 = $90.  \n   So he spent $90.\n\n3. **Selling the 5 CDs he didn't like**:  \n   He sells them for $40 total.\n\n4. **Net money out**:  \n   Money spent: $90  \n   Money recouped: $40  \n   Net loss: $90 \u2212 $40 = $50.\n\nAnswer: $50", "correct": true, "gold": "50"}
{"qid": "gsm:191", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "MAI-Thinking-1", "resp": "**Reasoning:** \r\n\r\n1. **Day 1:** Tobias ate $\\frac{2}{5}$ of 60 pieces. $\\frac{2}{5} \\times 60 = 24$ pieces. Remaining: $60 - 24 = 36$.\r\n2. **Day 2:** He ate 10 more pieces. Total so far: $24 + 10 = 34$. Remaining: $36 - 10 = 26$.\r\n3. **Day 3:** He ate $\\frac{7}{13}$ of the remaining 26 pieces. $\\frac{7}{13} \\times 26 = 14$ pieces. Total so far: $34 + 14 = 48$.\r\n\r\nAnswer: 48", "correct": true, "gold": "48"}
