{"qid": "gsm:193", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "The original price is $15 per CD. With a 40% discount, James pays 60% of that price, or $9 per CD.  \nFor all 10 CDs the total outlay is therefore \\(10 \\times 9 = \\$90\\).  \nHe later sells 5 of the CDs and receives $40 in return.  \nNet cash spent is \\(90 - 40 = \\$50\\).\n\nAnswer: $50", "correct": true, "gold": "50"}
{"qid": "gsm:192", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "MAI-Thinking-1", "resp": "**Reasoning:** \r\n\r\n1. **Total hats:** 100\r\n2. **Red hats:** Half of 100 = 50\r\n3. **Remaining after red:** 100 - 50 = 50\r\n4. **Blue hats:** 3/5 of the remaining = (3/5) \u00d7 50 = 30\r\n5. **White hats:** Remaining after blue = 50 - 30 = 20\r\n\r\nAnswer: 20", "correct": true, "gold": "20"}
{"qid": "gsm:193", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "Cohere-command-a-plus-05-2026", "resp": "<|START_TEXT|>James bought 10 CDs at $15 each, receiving a 40% discount.  \nDiscounted price per CD = $15\u202f\u00d7\u202f(1\u202f\u2013\u202f0.40) = $9.  \nTotal cost = 10\u202f\u00d7\u202f$9 = $90.  \n\nHe later sold 5 unwanted CDs for $40 total.  \n\nNet cash outflow = total cost \u2013 sale proceeds = $90\u202f\u2013\u202f$40 = $50.  \n\nAnswer: $50<|END_TEXT|>", "correct": true, "gold": "50"}
{"qid": "gsm:194", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "DeepSeek-V4-Flash", "resp": "We are given the area in square feet and the length in yards, so first convert the length to feet.\n\n1 yard = 3 feet, so length = 3 yards = 9 feet.\n\nArea = length \u00d7 width  \n360 = 9 \u00d7 width  \nwidth = 360 / 9 = 40 feet.\n\nPerimeter = 2 \u00d7 (length + width) = 2 \u00d7 (9 + 40) = 2 \u00d7 49 = 98 feet.\n\nAnswer: 98", "correct": true, "gold": "98"}
