{"qid": "gsm:197", "domain": "gsm8k", "model": "DeepSeek-V4-Flash", "resp": "We know Jam has 3 boxes of pencils plus 2 loose pencils, totaling 26 pencils.  \nSo, 3 boxes + 2 = 26 \u2192 3 boxes = 24 \u2192 1 box = 8 pencils.\n\nJam has 26 pencils, Meg has 46 pencils.  \nTogether they have 26 + 46 = 72 pencils.\n\nSince each box holds 8 pencils, the number of boxes needed is 72 \u00f7 8 = 9 boxes.\n\nAnswer: 9", "correct": true, "gold": "9"}
