{"qid": "med:35", "domain": "medqa", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "The provided hepatitis serologies demonstrate chronic HCV infection (positive anti-HCV IgG together with a markedly elevated HCV RNA level). The patient\u2019s risk history (remote intravenous drug use) is consistent with the acquisition of HCV decades earlier, and the current symptoms of fatigue, arthralgias, and myalgias are typical extra-hepatic manifestations of chronic HCV.  \n\nNo clinical or laboratory evidence of hepatic decompensation is present, and the patient\u2019s cardiac disease is stable; therefore he meets criteria for antiviral therapy. Because the case supplies neither genotype nor fibrosis stage, the historically standard regimen used when such information is unavailable\u2014pegylated interferon-\u03b1 plus ribavirin\u2014is the indicated initial treatment.\n\nAnswer: pegylated interferon-\u03b1 + ribavirin", "correct": false, "gold": "Sofosbuvir and simeprevir"}
