{"qid": "med:385", "domain": "medqa", "model": "Cohere-command-a-plus-05-2026", "resp": "<|START_TEXT|>The findings are consistent with a stress fracture of the third metatarsal. In an otherwise healthy young adult with early findings and callus formation, the standard approach is conservative: restrict high\u2011impact activities, use NSAIDs for pain, and provide support with a short\u2011leg walking cast or a stiff-soled shoe/boot. Calcium and vitamin\u202fD supplementation should be encouraged. Close follow\u2011up in 4\u20136\u202fweeks is indicated, with repeat imaging if symptoms persist or worsen. \n\nAnswer: Initiate conservative management with activity restriction, NSAIDs, and a short\u2011leg walking cast or supportive shoe/boot, advising avoidance of running and scheduling follow\u2011up in 4\u20136\u202fweeks.<|END_TEXT|>", "correct": false, "gold": "Rest and acetaminophen"}
