{"qid": "mp:8789", "domain": "mmlupro:math", "model": "openai/gpt-5.4", "resp": "First evaluate the parentheses:\n\n\\(8 - 5 = 3\\)\n\nThen compute left to right for multiplication and division:\n\n\\(6 \\cdot 24 = 144\\)\n\n\\(144 \\div 3 = 48\\)\n\nAnswer: 48", "correct": true, "gold": "48"}
{"qid": "mp:8854", "domain": "mmlupro:math", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "The binomial theorem expands \\((x + 2y)^7\\) via the general term\n\\[\n\\binom{7}{k} x^{7-k} (2y)^k = \\binom{7}{k} 2^k x^{7-k} y^k.\n\\]\nThe exponents required are \\(7-k=2\\) and \\(k=5\\), so \\(k=5\\). Substituting these values yields the term\n\\[\n\\binom{7}{5} \\cdot 2^5 \\cdot x^2 y^5.\n\\]\nBecause \\(\\binom{7}{5}=\\binom{7}{2}=21\\) and \\(2^5=32\\), the numerical coefficient is\n\\[\n21 \\times 32 = 672.\n\\]\n(The same coefficient is obtained by viewing the expansion as choosing 2 positions out of 7 for the factor \\(x\\) and multiplying by the constant \\(2^5\\) contributed by the remaining five factors of \\(2y\\).)\nAnswer: 672", "correct": true, "gold": "672"}
{"qid": "mp:7990", "domain": "mmlupro:math", "model": "MAI-Thinking-1", "resp": "Answer: $\\boxed{\\approx 4.61 \\times 10^{2}\\,\\text{minutes}}$", "correct": false, "gold": "460.5 min"}
{"qid": "mp:8789", "domain": "mmlupro:math", "model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5", "resp": "6 \u2022 24 = 144, then 144 \u00f7 (8\u22125) = 144 \u00f7 3 = 48\n\nAnswer: 48", "correct": true, "gold": "48"}
{"qid": "mp:8789", "domain": "mmlupro:math", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "First evaluate the expression inside the parentheses: $8 - 5 = 3$.\n\nThe expression becomes $6 \\cdot 24 \\div 3$.\n\nWorking from left to right with multiplication and division:\n$6 \\cdot 24 = 144$\n$144 \\div 3 = 48$\n\n(Alternatively: $24 \\div 3 = 8$, then $6 \\cdot 8 = 48$)\n\nAnswer: 48", "correct": true, "gold": "48"}
