{"qid": "mp:8531", "domain": "mmlupro:math", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "The heat flux is given by Fourier\u2019s law \\(\\mathbf q=-K\\nabla u\\).  \nFor \\(u=2y^{2}+2z^{2}\\) we have \\(\\nabla u=(0,4y,4z)\\).  \nThe outward unit normal to the cylinder \\(y^{2}+z^{2}=6\\) is \\(\\mathbf n=(0,y,z)/\\sqrt{6}\\).  \nHence  \n\\[\n\\nabla u\\cdot\\mathbf n=\\frac{4y^{2}+4z^{2}}{\\sqrt{6}}=\\frac{4\\cdot6}{\\sqrt{6}}=4\\sqrt6,\n\\]\nwhich is constant on the surface.  \n\nThe lateral surface area of the cylinder (radius \\(\\sqrt6\\), height \\(4\\)) is  \n\\[\nA=2\\pi\\sqrt6\\cdot4=8\\pi\\sqrt6.\n\\]\n\nThe rate of heat flow **inward** is  \n\\[\n\\iint_S \\mathbf q\\cdot(-\\mathbf n)\\,dS\n=K\\iint_S \\nabla u\\cdot\\mathbf n\\,dS\n=K\\,(4\\sqrt6)\\,(8\\pi\\sqrt6)\n=K\\cdot192\\pi.\n\\]\n\nWith \\(K=6.5\\),\n\\[\n6.5\\times192\\pi=1248\\pi.\n\\]\n\n(The flux through the end caps is zero because \\(\\nabla u\\) has no \\(x\\)-component.)\n\nAnswer: 1248\u03c0", "correct": true, "gold": "$1248\\pi$"}
{"qid": "mp:8104", "domain": "mmlupro:math", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "The order of any permutation \\(\\sigma \\in S_n\\) is completely determined by its cycle type: if \\(\\sigma\\) decomposes into disjoint cycles of lengths \\(\\ell_1,\\dots,\\ell_k\\), then\n\\[\n\\operatorname{ord}(\\sigma)=\\operatorname{lcm}(\\ell_1,\\dots,\\ell_k).\n\\]\nConsequently the maximal order in \\(S_n\\) is the maximum value of this LCM over all partitions of the integer \\(n\\).\nFor \\(n=6\\) the partitions and the corresponding LCM values are:\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n6 &\\mapsto 6,\\\\\n5+1 &\\mapsto 5,\\\\\n4+2 &\\mapsto 4,\\\\\n4+1+1 &\\mapsto 4,\\\\\n3+3 &\\mapsto 3,\\\\\n3+2+1 &\\mapsto 6,\\\\\n3+1+1+1 &\\mapsto 3,\\\\\n2+2+2 &\\mapsto 2,\\\\\n2+2+1+1 &\\mapsto 2,\\\\\n2+1+1+1+1 &\\mapsto 2,\\\\\n1+1+1+1+1+1 &\\mapsto 1.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\nThe largest entry in the right-hand column is 6, attained by the partitions \\((6)\\) and \\((3,2,1)\\). Hence the maximal order of an element of \\(S_6\\) is exactly 6.\n(Explicit representatives are any 6-cycle, e.g. \\((1\\,2\\,3\\,4\\,5\\,6)\\), and any product of a disjoint 3-cycle and transposition, e.g. \\((1\\,2\\,3)(4\\,5)\\).)\nAnswer: 6", "correct": true, "gold": "6"}
