{"qid": "mp:8104", "domain": "mmlupro:math", "model": "Cohere-command-a-plus-05-2026", "resp": "<|START_TEXT|>To maximize the order of a permutation in \\(S_6\\), we consider the least common multiple (LCM) of the lengths of its disjoint cycles, since the order of a permutation equals this LCM.  \n\nPossible cycle type partitions of 6 and their LCMs are:\n\n- \\(6\\)\u2003\u2192\u2003LCM\\(=6\\)  \n- \\(5+1\\)\u2003\u2192\u2003LCM\\(=5\\)  \n- \\(4+2\\)\u2003\u2192\u2003LCM\\(=4\\)  \n- \\(4+1+1\\)\u2003\u2192\u2003LCM\\(=4\\)  \n- \\(3+3\\)\u2003\u2192\u2003LCM\\(=3\\)  \n- \\(3+2+1\\)\u2003\u2192\u2003LCM\\(=6\\)  \n- Other partitions give LCMs \\(\\le 3\\).\n\nThe largest LCM obtained is \\(6\\), achieved either by a single 6\u2011cycle or by a disjoint 3\u2011cycle and 2\u2011cycle.\n\nAnswer: 6<|END_TEXT|>", "correct": true, "gold": "6"}
