{"qid": "mp:8604", "domain": "mmlupro:math", "model": "DeepSeek-V4-Flash", "resp": "We are given the parametric equations:\n\n\\[\nx(t) = 4\\cos t + \\cos(12t), \\quad y(t) = 4\\sin t + \\sin(12t)\n\\]\n\nUpward velocity is the vertical component of velocity, which is \\(\\frac{dy}{dt}\\).\n\nDifferentiate \\(y(t)\\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{dy}{dt} = 4\\cos t + 12\\cos(12t)\n\\]\n\nAt \\(t = 1\\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{dy}{dt}\\bigg|_{t=1} = 4\\cos(1) + 12\\cos(12)\n\\]\n\nThis is the upward velocity at \\(t=1\\).\n\nAnswer: \\(4\\cos(1) + 12\\cos(12)\\)", "correct": false, "gold": "12.287"}
{"qid": "mp:8604", "domain": "mmlupro:math", "model": "openai/gpt-5.4", "resp": "Differentiate the parametric equations to get the velocity components:\n\n\\[\nx(t)=4\\cos t+\\cos(12t), \\quad y(t)=4\\sin t+\\sin(12t)\n\\]\n\nSo\n\n\\[\n\\frac{dx}{dt}=-4\\sin t-12\\sin(12t)\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=4\\cos t+12\\cos(12t)\n\\]\n\n\u201cUpward velocity\u201d means the vertical component of velocity, so evaluate \\(\\frac{dy}{dt}\\) at \\(t=1\\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{dy}{dt}\\Big|_{t=1}=4\\cos(1)+12\\cos(12)\n\\]\n\nUsing radians,\n\n\\[\n4\\cos(1)+12\\cos(12)\\approx 4(0.5403)+12(0.8439)\\approx 2.1612+10.1268=12.288\n\\]\n\nAnswer: \\(\\displaystyle 4\\cos(1)+12\\cos(12)\\approx 12.288\\)", "correct": true, "gold": "12.287"}
{"qid": "mp:8604", "domain": "mmlupro:math", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "The upward velocity of the satellite is the rate of change of its vertical position coordinate. Given the parametric equation\n\\[\ny = 4\\sin(t) + \\sin(12t),\n\\]\ndifferentiate with respect to the parameter \\(t\\):\n\\[\n\\frac{dy}{dt} = 4\\cos(t) + 12\\cos(12t).\n\\]\nEvaluating the derivative at the required instant \\(t=1\\) produces the exact value\n\\[\n4\\cos(1)+12\\cos(12).\n\\]\n(The angle arguments are understood to be in radians, the standard mathematical convention.)\n\nAnswer: 4 cos(1) + 12 cos(12)", "correct": false, "gold": "12.287"}
{"qid": "mp:8604", "domain": "mmlupro:math", "model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5", "resp": "# Finding the Upward Velocity\n\n## Setting Up the Derivative\n\nThe upward velocity refers to the vertical component of velocity, which is dy/dt.\n\nGiven: y = 4sin(t) + sin(12t)\n\nTaking the derivative with respect to t:\n\n$$\\frac{dy}{dt} = 4\\cos(t) + 12\\cos(12t)$$\n\n## Evaluating at t = 1\n\n$$\\frac{dy}{dt}\\bigg|_{t=1} = 4\\cos(1) + 12\\cos(12)$$\n\n**Calculating each term** (using radians):\n- cos(1) \u2248 0.5403\n- cos(12) \u2248 0.8439\n\n**Substituting:**\n$$\\frac{dy}{dt}\\bigg|_{t=1} = 4(0.5403) + 12(0.8439)$$\n\n$$= 2.1612 + 10.1268$$\n\n$$= 12.288$$\n\nAnswer: dy/dt \u2248 12.288 (using dy/dt = 4cos(1) + 12cos(12))", "correct": true, "gold": "12.287"}
{"qid": "mp:7839", "domain": "mmlupro:math", "model": "grok-4.3", "resp": "The given equation can be rearranged and simplified as follows:\n\\[\n2x^2 + 2y^2 - 12x + 4y - 20 = 0.\n\\]\nDividing through by 2 yields\n\\[\nx^2 + y^2 - 6x + 2y - 10 = 0.\n\\]\nCompleting the square for the \\(x\\)- and \\(y\\)-terms produces\n\\[\n(x-3)^2 + (y+1)^2 = 20.\n\\]\nThis is the equation of a circle with center \\((3,-1)\\) and radius \\(\\sqrt{20} = 2\\sqrt{5}\\).\nA circle inscribed in a square is tangent to all four sides of the square. Consequently, the diameter of the circle equals the side length of the square:\n\\[\n2\\sqrt{20} = 4\\sqrt{5}.\n\\]\n(The given condition that a pair of sides is parallel to the \\(x\\)-axis forces the square to be axis-aligned, but the side length equals the diameter for any orientation of the square.) The area of the square is therefore\n\\[\n(4\\sqrt{5})^2 = 80.\n\\]\nAnswer: 80", "correct": true, "gold": "80"}
{"qid": "mp:8402", "domain": "mmlupro:math", "model": "Cohere-command-a-plus-05-2026", "resp": "<|START_TEXT|>To seat 10 distinct people at identical round tables (any number of tables, each non\u2011empty), each seating arrangement corresponds to a permutation of the 10 people: each cycle of the permutation gives the circular order at one table, and tables are unlabeled. Hence the total number of arrangements equals the number of permutations of 10 objects:\n\n\\(10! = 3{,}628{,}800\\).\n\nAnswer: 3628800<|END_TEXT|>", "correct": false, "gold": "362880"}
