{"qid": "mp:7692", "domain": "mmlupro:math", "model": "MAI-Thinking-1", "resp": "Brief reason:\n- Statement 1: $159 = 3 \\cdot 53$ with $3 \\nmid (53-1)=52$. For distinct primes $p<q$ and $p \\nmid q-1$, every group of order $pq$ is cyclic. Thus true.\n- Statement 2: $102 = 2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 17$. The number $n_{17}$ of Sylow 17-subgroups satisfies $n_{17} \\equiv 1 \\pmod{17}$ and $n_{17} \\mid 6$, so $n_{17}=1$. Hence the unique Sylow 17-subgroup is a nontrivial proper normal subgroup. Thus true.\n\nAnswer: Both statements are true.", "correct": false, "gold": "True, True"}
{"qid": "mp:9001", "domain": "mmlupro:math", "model": "Kimi-K2.5", "resp": "First, find the daily migration rate of the humpback whales:  \n$2,240 \\text{ miles} \\div 28 \\text{ days} = 80 \\text{ miles per day}$.\n\nNext, calculate how far the humpback whales would travel in 32 days at that rate:  \n$80 \\text{ miles/day} \\times 32 \\text{ days} = 2,560 \\text{ miles}$.\n\nFinally, subtract the gray whales' distance from this amount:  \n$2,560 \\text{ miles} - 2,368 \\text{ miles} = 192 \\text{ miles}$.\n\nAnswer: 192", "correct": true, "gold": "192"}
